日期: 2025-08-05

1
00:00:21,480 --> 00:00:23,960
《星际迷航：新世界》前情提要
Previously on Star Trek: Strange New Worlds...

2
00:00:23,960 --> 00:00:24,660
佩利亚中校
Commander Pelia,

3
00:00:24,660 --> 00:00:26,280
这是斯考特上尉 他需要你的帮助
this is Lieutenant Scott. He needs your help.

4
00:00:26,280 --> 00:00:27,980
我认识斯考特
I know Scotty.

5
00:00:27,980 --> 00:00:29,240
教授
Professor.

6
00:00:30,280 --> 00:00:31,340
在人类文化中
Is it not tradition

7
00:00:31,340 --> 00:00:32,660
隆重的浪漫表达 难道不是传统吗
to make a grand romantic gesture,

8
00:00:33,540 --> 00:00:36,070
还是我又对人类的关系产生误解了
or have I again mistaken how human relationships work?

9
00:00:36,860 --> 00:00:37,738
你和克莉丝汀不是决定
I thought you and Christine

10
00:00:37,738 --> 00:00:39,620
暂时分开 给彼此一点个人空间吗
had decided to give each other some space.

11
00:00:39,620 --> 00:00:40,460
确实
Indeed.

12
00:00:42,520 --> 00:00:43,100
史波克
Spock.

13
00:00:43,100 --> 00:00:43,940
克莉丝汀
Christine.

14
00:00:43,940 --> 00:00:46,500
这是科尔比博士
This is... Dr. Korby.

15
00:00:47,540 --> 00:00:48,960
我的约会对象
My date.

16
00:01:00,740 --> 00:01:01,862
舰长
Captain,

17
00:01:01,862 --> 00:01:04,332
我们又探测到了那个太空辐射
we're picking up that space radiation again.

18
00:01:06,167 --> 00:01:07,835
无论如何
Whatever this is

19
00:01:07,835 --> 00:01:10,838
它都不像是布鲁塔星云的本土产物
does not appear to be native to the Blootar Nebula.

20
00:01:11,600 --> 00:01:14,140
这是在太空 上尉
This is space, Lieutenant.

21
00:01:14,140 --> 00:01:17,580
没有什么所谓的 本土
There's no such thing as... native.

22
00:01:17,580 --> 00:01:20,880
我们都是宇宙的孩子
We're all children... of the cosmos.

23
00:01:20,880 --> 00:01:23,000
舰长 在过去一小时内
Cap, in the past hour,

24
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:25,085
我们又有十四名船员
we have had 14 more crew members report

25
00:01:25,085 --> 00:01:27,860
因忧郁症去医务室报道
to medbay on account of melancholia.

26
00:01:27,860 --> 00:01:29,457
我这辈子只见过一次这种场面
I have seen this only once before...

27
00:01:30,280 --> 00:01:31,820
在战场上
in the war.

28
00:01:31,820 --> 00:01:33,080
那我们需要点帮助了
Then we'll need a leg up.

29
00:01:34,020 --> 00:01:36,020
但是舰长 我们不在管制星域内啊
But Captain, we're outside of regulation space.

30
00:01:36,020 --> 00:01:39,940
跟我谈管辖权你还太嫩了 上尉
Don't lecture me on jurisdiction, Lieutenant!

31
00:01:39,940 --> 00:01:44,605
太空管辖权的书 可是我编的
I wrote the book on space... jurisdiction.

32
00:01:45,880 --> 00:01:48,409
而我最出名的可就是
And I am known for my...

33
00:01:49,380 --> 00:01:50,411
语言措辞
diction.

34
00:01:51,600 --> 00:01:52,935
好了
Now...

35
00:01:54,700 --> 00:01:57,918
给我联系 艾戈尼亚人
...get me... the Agonyans.

36
00:01:58,853 --> 00:02:02,590
艾戈尼亚人是极其危险的太空生物
The Agonyans are extremely dangerous space creatures.

37
00:02:02,590 --> 00:02:04,600
你以为我不知道吗
You don't think I know that?!

38
00:02:04,600 --> 00:02:07,160
联系他们 上尉
Make the call, Lieutenant,

39
00:02:07,160 --> 00:02:10,564
为了布鲁塔星云和太空
for the sake of the Blootar Nebula and space.

40
00:02:12,820 --> 00:02:15,736
舰长 太空电话接通艾戈尼亚人了
Captain, I have the Agonyans on the space-phone.

41
00:02:15,736 --> 00:02:17,505
放到屏幕上
On viewer-screen.

42
00:02:18,972 --> 00:02:21,160
联盟星舰冒险号向您问好
Greetings from the USS Adventure.

43
00:02:21,160 --> 00:02:24,100
我 便是这艘船的舰长
I am... the captain of this vessel,

44
00:02:24,100 --> 00:02:27,400
代表整个外太空行星联盟
representing the whole of the Alliance of Outer Space Planets.

45
00:02:27,400 --> 00:02:31,652
我是兹普诺普 来自艾戈尼亚三元帝国
I am Zipnop of the Triathic Agonyan Empire.

46
00:02:31,652 --> 00:02:37,620
崇拜我们吧 渺小可悲的人类粮堆
All worship to us, small, pathetic, human food-piles.

47
00:02:37,620 --> 00:02:40,640
我们在布鲁塔星云里检测到了
We scanned an unusual level of radiation

48
00:02:40,640 --> 00:02:42,240
水平异常的辐射
in the Blootar Nebula.

49
00:02:42,240 --> 00:02:47,140
尽管这是在贵国的管辖区外
Even though this is outside of your empire's... jurisdiction.

50
00:02:47,140 --> 00:02:48,869
好一个弥天大谎
That is a lie!

51
00:02:48,869 --> 00:02:51,600
可悲却美味的人类们四散的谣言
Spread by pathetic but delicious humans.

52
00:02:51,600 --> 00:02:53,940
但是 医生
And yet... Doctor,

53
00:02:53,940 --> 00:02:56,740
我们的船上不是出现了大量的
have we not received multiple cases of melancholia

54
00:02:56,740 --> 00:02:58,060
忧郁症病例吗
aboard this ship?

55
00:02:58,060 --> 00:02:59,060
没错 舰长
We have, Cap.

56
00:02:59,060 --> 00:03:01,220
忧郁症不是只有在人类接触到
And doesn't melancholia only occur

57
00:03:01,220 --> 00:03:04,220
艾戈尼亚辐射时 才会发病吗
when humans are exposed to Agonyan radiation waves?

58
00:03:04,220 --> 00:03:05,120
的确如此
True.

59
00:03:05,120 --> 00:03:07,840
将 死
Check and... mate.

60
00:03:07,840 --> 00:03:11,380
啊 你发现了我们的计划
Argh! You have figured out our plan.

61
00:03:11,380 --> 00:03:14,680
就算我们需要你们的脑细胞来给辐射供能
We may need your brain cells to power our radiation,

62
00:03:14,680 --> 00:03:16,697
但你们绝对阻止不了我们
but you will never stop us!

63
00:03:16,697 --> 00:03:18,899
没门 因为我们必须阻止你们
We can, and we will because we must.

64
00:03:19,420 --> 00:03:22,560
这是我们星际探险家的职责
It is our duty... as space explorers.

65
00:03:22,560 --> 00:03:24,572
没机会了 我们要先灭了你
Not if we destroy you first.

66
00:03:24,572 --> 00:03:26,160
我倒要看你怎么灭
I'd like to see you try.

67
00:03:26,160 --> 00:03:27,880
但是舰长 要是被他们得逞了怎么办
But Captain, what if they can?

68
00:03:27,880 --> 00:03:30,520
你们人类有很多脑细胞
You humans are rich with brain cells.

69
00:03:31,160 --> 00:03:32,880
只要你们给我们脑细胞
If you give them to us,

70
00:03:32,880 --> 00:03:35,700
我们就可以不毁灭你们
we will choose not to destroy you.

71
00:03:36,305 --> 00:03:38,140
给你们一分钟的时间
You have one minute to 

72
00:03:38,140 --> 00:03:40,288
来满足我们的要求
comply with our wishes.

73
00:03:41,589 --> 00:03:45,559
艾戈尼亚人把我们逼上了绝路
The Agonyans have put us in an impossible situation.

74
00:03:46,327 --> 00:03:48,760
只剩一条出路了
There is... only one solution.

75
00:03:49,180 --> 00:03:51,599
绝不能给出我们的脑细胞
We can't give them our brain cells.

76
00:03:52,460 --> 00:03:54,955
从科学角度讲 我们需要脑细胞
We need it... for many science reasons.

77
00:03:56,840 --> 00:03:58,660
舰长 艾戈尼亚人
Captain, the Agonyans

78
00:03:58,660 --> 00:04:01,840
正在向我们发射核能激光
are firing a series of nuclear lasers at us.

79
00:04:01,840 --> 00:04:03,577
升起护盾 准备迎接冲击
Shields up! Brace for impact!

80
00:04:11,719 --> 00:04:13,787
用光子射线还击
Fire photonos beams at them!

81
00:04:17,840 --> 00:04:19,012
他们走了
They're gone.

82
00:04:20,100 --> 00:04:22,400
随之而去的还有
And so is...

83
00:04:22,400 --> 00:04:24,140
-我们的脑细胞 -不
- our brain cells. - No!

84
00:04:24,140 --> 00:04:25,366
我们怎么办
What do we do?

85
00:04:29,060 --> 00:04:32,396
首先 我们找到艾戈尼亚人
First... we find the Agonyans...

86
00:04:33,460 --> 00:04:36,180
拿回我们的脑细胞
...retrieve our... brain cells,

87
00:04:36,180 --> 00:04:37,620
然后
and then...

88
00:04:37,620 --> 00:04:39,760
找回我们的快乐
we get back our joy.

89
00:04:44,520 --> 00:04:47,060
银河系 人类最后的边疆
Galaxies: the last frontier.

90
00:04:47,060 --> 00:04:49,640
这是联盟星舰冒险号的故事
This is the tale of the USS Adventure

91
00:04:49,640 --> 00:04:51,800
她长达八十四个月的任务
on its 84-month mission

92
00:04:51,800 --> 00:04:55,580
去迷航至宇宙最遥远的角落
as it treks across the furthest reaches of the universe,

93
00:04:55,580 --> 00:04:57,740
去努力寻找未知生命
striving to find unknown life,

94
00:04:57,740 --> 00:05:02,060
未解之谜 与未至之地
unexplained phenomena, and new space destinations.

95
00:05:02,060 --> 00:05:04,640
勇往直前 超越极限
To go forward, to go beyond,

96
00:05:04,640 --> 00:05:07,441
更勇敢地踏足更加遥远的未竟之地
to go further and bolder than anyone ever before.

97
00:05:49,060 --> 00:05:51,240
安全官日志
Security Officer's Log.

98
00:05:51,240 --> 00:05:54,154
进取号即将穿过基托利安带
Enterprise is about to pass through the Kitolian Belt,

99
00:05:54,154 --> 00:05:56,156
其环绕着的中心是一颗中子星
which centers on a neutron star.

100
00:05:56,620 --> 00:05:59,527
不过在进取号研究中子星的时候
But while Enterprise studies the neutron star,

101
00:05:59,527 --> 00:06:03,580
我被安排了另一项同等重要的工作
I've been assigned a separate but equally important task.

102
00:06:03,580 --> 00:06:07,601
算它作双重任务吧
Call it a dual mission.

103
00:06:09,640 --> 00:06:12,880
您是想让我去玩游戏吗 长官
You want me to... play a game, sir?

104
00:06:12,880 --> 00:06:14,642
星际舰队觉得他们找到了
Starfleet believes that they have figured out

105
00:06:14,642 --> 00:06:17,080
能够进行长期超光速旅行的方法
 a solution to long-term, faster-than-light travel.

106
00:06:17,080 --> 00:06:19,300
不用多久 星舰就可以持续巡航五年以上
Starships will soon be able to go for more

107
00:06:19,300 --> 00:06:21,340
而不用中途返回联邦
than five years without returning to Federation.

108
00:06:21,340 --> 00:06:23,300
为了散心和释放压力
So, games and entertainment as

109
00:06:23,300 --> 00:06:25,480
我们需要游戏和娱乐
distraction and stress release.

110
00:06:25,480 --> 00:06:27,387
这个我们要测试的设备是叫做
Now the device we're going to be testing is called

111
00:06:27,387 --> 00:06:29,520
「娱乐室」
the "Re-creation Room"?

112
00:06:29,520 --> 00:06:31,460
简称 全息甲板
Holodeck, for short.

113
00:06:31,460 --> 00:06:32,640
-这个好听 -没错
- Sounds better. - Yeah.

114
00:06:32,640 --> 00:06:35,140
这东西是基于战斗模拟器改进的吗
Is this based on battle simulators?

115
00:06:35,140 --> 00:06:36,860
毕竟 模拟器每一关我全都打过了
'Cause I-I've beaten every one of those.

116
00:06:36,860 --> 00:06:38,740
不然为什么我们选你呢
Why do you think we picked you?

117
00:06:38,740 --> 00:06:41,000
但是这种模拟器通常都设在星站上
But those simulators are usually on starbases.

118
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:43,437
它会占用大量的能量和算力
They take up huge amounts of energy and processing power.

119
00:06:44,460 --> 00:06:45,860
我们的船真的撑得起来吗
Can our ship actually handle it?

120
00:06:45,860 --> 00:06:47,741
我们就是来搞明白这一点的
That's what we're here to figure out.

121
00:06:47,741 --> 00:06:49,500
我们的命令很明确
Our orders are clear.

122
00:06:49,500 --> 00:06:51,360
在进取号研究坍缩中子星的同时
While Enterprise studies the collapsing neutron star,

123
00:06:51,360 --> 00:06:53,520
你要来测试全息甲板
you're going to test the holodeck.

124
00:06:53,520 --> 00:06:55,360
实战测试一下它能不能在出任务时启用
Put it through its paces under a real mission.

125
00:06:55,360 --> 00:06:58,460
证明它能在真实的 严苛的环境下运作
Show it could work under genuine, rigorous circumstances.

126
00:06:58,460 --> 00:07:02,022
您觉得一场游戏对全息甲板来说能有多严苛 长官
How rigorous do you expect a game on the holodeck to be, sir?

127
00:07:03,140 --> 00:07:05,640
嘛 这是个测试 上尉
Well, it's a test, Lieutenant.

128
00:07:05,640 --> 00:07:06,960
我以前当试飞员的时候
The kind of thing I'd do all the time

129
00:07:06,960 --> 00:07:08,020
对测试只有一种态度
when I was a test pilot.

130
00:07:08,020 --> 00:07:09,296
意思就是
Which means,

131
00:07:10,200 --> 00:07:12,140
往死里测试它
you push it as hard as you can.

132
00:07:13,020 --> 00:07:14,968
你跟我说过你想要点挑战
You told me you needed a challenge.

133
00:07:16,080 --> 00:07:17,204
不用谢
You're welcome.

134
00:07:29,840 --> 00:07:31,485
我打扰你了吗
Am I interrupting?

135
00:07:31,485 --> 00:07:33,760
我选择用舞蹈训练代替
In lieu of my normal morning calisthenics,

136
00:07:33,760 --> 00:07:35,540
我每天早上的体操运动
I have elected to continue dance training.

137
00:07:35,540 --> 00:07:37,000
已经差不多要结束了
I have nearly completed my routine.

138
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:38,526
噢 我来了你也不用停啊
Oh, don't stop on my account.

139
00:07:41,700 --> 00:07:44,103
计算机 播放歌单 史波克十九号
Computer, begin playlist: Spock 19.

140
00:07:48,920 --> 00:07:50,740
探戈
Tango.

141
00:07:50,740 --> 00:07:52,472
很上进啊
Ambitious.

142
00:07:53,520 --> 00:07:55,740
我只是顺道来问一下 斯考提让你修的
I just swung by to ask about the field emitters

143
00:07:55,740 --> 00:07:58,178
全息甲板力场发射器现在怎么样了
for the holodeck that you've been fixing for Scotty?

144
00:08:00,020 --> 00:08:01,327
抬眼 上尉
Eyes up, Lieutenant.

145
00:08:02,760 --> 00:08:04,852
你之前对我说 眼神是探戈生根的地方
You told me the eyes are the anchor of the tango.

146
00:08:04,852 --> 00:08:06,160
不是吗
Are they not?

147
00:08:14,820 --> 00:08:16,900
我的诊断分析差不多都完成了
My diagnostics are nearly complete.

148
00:08:16,900 --> 00:08:18,520
力场发射器都已经重新校准完毕
I have realigned the field emitters.

149
00:08:18,960 --> 00:08:20,780
你和斯考特先生只要设计好程序
The holodeck should be operational as soon as you and 

150
00:08:20,780 --> 00:08:23,080
全息甲板即可投入运行
Mr. Scott finish designing a program for you.

151
00:08:23,080 --> 00:08:23,940
谢谢
Thank you.

152
00:08:24,300 --> 00:08:26,106
戴着监控针会让你难受吗
Has the monitoring pin been much of a burden?

153
00:08:26,106 --> 00:08:28,300
我都忘了自己还戴着这东西
I actually forgot I was wearing it.

154
00:08:28,300 --> 00:08:30,243
这是好事
That is a good thing.

155
00:08:30,243 --> 00:08:32,320
能捕捉到你自然的状态是最好的
It is best if it captures you in a natural state,

156
00:08:32,320 --> 00:08:34,200
这样全息甲板就能根据你的参数
so the holodeck can construct the most realistic environment

157
00:08:34,200 --> 00:08:35,783
营造出最逼真的环境
for your specifications.

158
00:08:36,880 --> 00:08:39,440
说到这里 你选好全息模拟的主题了吗
Speaking of, have you chosen a subject for your simulation?

159
00:08:40,180 --> 00:08:41,054
还没呢
Not yet.

160
00:08:42,960 --> 00:08:44,840
我对人类娱乐领域涉猎未深
I am not well-versed in human entertainment,

161
00:08:44,840 --> 00:08:47,160
不过暴力与休闲的主题似乎比较热门
but violence and relaxation seem to be popular.

162
00:08:48,440 --> 00:08:49,797
此外
Along with...

163
00:08:52,100 --> 00:08:53,620
浪漫故事亦是如此
...romantic narratives.

164
00:08:59,560 --> 00:09:01,341
艾米莉亚
Amelia.

165
00:09:01,341 --> 00:09:04,100
《艾米莉亚·穆恩》是什么鬼
Amelia Moon? What the hell is that?

166
00:09:04,100 --> 00:09:06,860
20世纪60年代的地球侦探小说
Detective stories from Earth in the 1960s.

167
00:09:06,860 --> 00:09:09,680
那位把我从戈恩人手里救出来的舰长
The-the captain of the ship that rescued me from the Gorn-- 

168
00:09:09,680 --> 00:09:11,020
给了我一本
he-he gave me a copy,

169
00:09:11,020 --> 00:09:13,820
看得我爱不释手
and I became obsessed.

170
00:09:14,600 --> 00:09:17,520
艾米莉亚是个局外人 但她总是莫名地
Amelia was an outsider, but she always found herself

171
00:09:17,520 --> 00:09:20,200
被卷入各种谋杀案 绑架案
in the middle of a murder, or a kidnapping,

172
00:09:20,200 --> 00:09:22,362
或者闹了什么乌龙的抢劫案
or a heist gone wrong.

173
00:09:23,100 --> 00:09:25,700
但她总是能伸张正义
And she always got justice,

174
00:09:25,700 --> 00:09:27,120
无论情况如何
no matter what.

175
00:09:29,002 --> 00:09:30,880
这么说吧
Let's just say...

176
00:09:30,880 --> 00:09:31,940
我被她带坏了
she had an effect on me.

177
00:09:32,480 --> 00:09:34,640
数据库里找到了112项结果
There are 112 of them in the database.

178
00:09:34,640 --> 00:09:36,720
这些内容拿来建立模拟绰绰有余了
That's plenty of material to form the simulation.

179
00:09:36,720 --> 00:09:38,680
不过要让模拟就这么一直运行下去
Although, the computer might have trouble 

180
00:09:38,680 --> 00:09:41,840
计算机会有点吃力
keeping the simulation running as it is.

181
00:09:41,840 --> 00:09:43,340
考虑到佩利亚离舰休假了
Uh, Pelia's on shore leave,

182
00:09:43,340 --> 00:09:44,720
所以你的意思是 又要请史波克出马了
so, you-you want to call in Spock again?

183
00:09:45,880 --> 00:09:47,260
小事一桩 我搞得定
It's nothing I can't handle.

184
00:09:47,260 --> 00:09:49,360
我能把全舰其他系统
I-I can balance the processing needs

185
00:09:49,360 --> 00:09:50,660
的处理需求给匀过来
from the rest of the ship.

186
00:09:51,160 --> 00:09:53,280
不过 有个小问题
Although, there is one wee wrinkle.

187
00:09:53,280 --> 00:09:55,560
呃 全息投影的角色
Uh, the holographic characters

188
00:09:55,560 --> 00:09:58,560
必须做到纤毫毕现才够格
need to be incredibly detailed to pass muster.

189
00:09:58,560 --> 00:10:02,060
分辨率这么高的生命特征数据
The only bio-signatures we have at that resolution

190
00:10:02,060 --> 00:10:03,600
我们只在传送器模式缓冲区里有
are from the transporter pattern buffer.

191
00:10:03,600 --> 00:10:05,180
我们会利用他们的形象
We'll use their likenesses

192
00:10:05,180 --> 00:10:07,407
来创造全息可交互角色
to create holographic interactive avatars.

193
00:10:07,860 --> 00:10:09,380
就等你准备好了 上尉
Ready when you are, Lieutenant.

194
00:10:12,660 --> 00:10:16,660
计算机 以艾米莉亚·穆恩系列小说为参考
Computer: using the Amelia Moon novels as reference

195
00:10:16,660 --> 00:10:20,040
并根据我自身的侦探水平
and factoring in my skills as an investigator,

196
00:10:20,800 --> 00:10:24,992
创造一个我难以解决的悬疑故事
create a new mystery that I will find challenging to solve.

197
00:10:33,640 --> 00:10:34,960
史波克 我
Spock, I...

198
00:10:34,960 --> 00:10:36,680
我以为你已经完成诊断分析了
I thought you'd finished running diagnostics.

199
00:10:36,680 --> 00:10:39,180
我想确保计算机系统能在
I wanted to ensure the computer system is functioning

200
00:10:39,180 --> 00:10:40,240
正常参数内运行
at normal parameters.

201
00:10:40,240 --> 00:10:41,980
多谢你的关心
I appreciate your concern.

202
00:10:41,980 --> 00:10:44,440
但是 不要告诉斯考提
But, uh, don't tell Scotty.

203
00:10:44,440 --> 00:10:45,760
他为了这事忙得累死累活的
He's been working very hard on this.

204
00:10:45,760 --> 00:10:47,860
确实 他很敏感
Indeed. He is sensitive.

205
00:10:48,620 --> 00:10:51,418
你随时都可启动并评估该程序
You may run and evaluate the program on your command.

206
00:10:54,020 --> 00:10:55,923
计算机
Computer:

207
00:10:55,923 --> 00:10:57,257
运行程序
...run program.

208
00:11:03,860 --> 00:11:06,160
我能真的闻到大海和香烟的味道
I can practically smell the ocean and the cigarettes.

209
00:11:06,160 --> 00:11:08,540
在全息甲板的有限空间内吸烟并非明智之举
It would be unwise to smoke in the confines of the holodeck.

210
00:11:08,540 --> 00:11:09,860
或者说 吸烟本就不明智
Or at all.

211
00:11:09,860 --> 00:11:11,600
不 我只是觉得这 这真是太
No. I just meant it's-it's very, um...

212
00:11:11,600 --> 00:11:12,720
栩栩如生
Lifelike.

213
00:11:13,540 --> 00:11:14,660
确实如此
Indeed.

214
00:11:14,660 --> 00:11:18,380
我读了那么久的艾米莉亚啊 我只是
I have spent so many hours reading about Amelia. I just...

215
00:11:18,380 --> 00:11:20,848
我不敢相信我真的能亲身扮演她
I just can't believe I actually get to be her.

216
00:11:20,848 --> 00:11:22,682
好吧 正如我的祖先
Well, as my ancestor,

217
00:11:22,682 --> 00:11:24,480
阿瑟·柯南·道尔爵士会写的那样
Sir Arthur Conan Doyle would write,

218
00:11:24,480 --> 00:11:25,700
「游戏开始了」
"The game is afoot."

219
00:11:26,680 --> 00:11:28,340
谢谢 史波克先生
Thank you, Mr. Spock,

220
00:11:28,340 --> 00:11:30,290
但这是个单人档
but this is a single-player situation.

221
00:11:31,200 --> 00:11:32,340
随时为你效劳
I am available,

222
00:11:32,340 --> 00:11:34,460
需要我的帮助就随时叫我
should you decide you need my assistance.

223
00:11:34,460 --> 00:11:36,000
祝你好运 上尉
Good luck, Lieutenant.

224
00:11:39,820 --> 00:11:41,420
艾米莉亚·穆恩
Amelia Moon!

225
00:11:41,420 --> 00:11:43,203
-谢天谢地你来了 -乌乎拉
- Thank goodness you're here. - Uhura.

226
00:11:43,203 --> 00:11:44,838
乔尼·格洛斯 我们在去年十一月
Joni Gloss. We met briefly

227
00:11:44,838 --> 00:11:46,974
你解决那起福克斯惨案的时候有过一面之缘
when you handled that Fox fiasco last November.

228
00:11:46,974 --> 00:11:48,375
你保住了我的客户的事业
Saved my client's career,

229
00:11:48,375 --> 00:11:49,780
才让他没被关进圣昆汀监狱
and kept him out of San Quentin.

230
00:11:49,780 --> 00:11:50,980
好了 跟我来
 Now, follow me.

231
00:11:50,980 --> 00:11:52,180
是我发现了尸体
I'm the one who found the body.

232
00:11:52,180 --> 00:11:53,546
不是我还能是谁
Of course, I did.

233
00:11:53,546 --> 00:11:54,840
我总是第一个到
I'm always the first to arrive.

234
00:11:54,840 --> 00:11:56,200
在这座城里我有条规矩
And I have a rule in this town.

235
00:11:56,200 --> 00:11:57,560
如果你准时 那你就迟到了
If you're on time, you're late.

236
00:11:57,560 --> 00:11:59,080
如果你迟到了 你就死定了
And if you're late, you're dead.

237
00:11:59,860 --> 00:12:02,520
现在好了 真的死人了
In this case, literally.

238
00:12:02,520 --> 00:12:04,240
当然 这可不是我干的
Not by my hand, of course.

239
00:12:04,240 --> 00:12:05,220
你会记下这句话的吧
You'll put that in your record?

240
00:12:07,200 --> 00:12:10,263
不过 你不是第一个到的客人 对吧
Only, you weren't the first guest to arrive, were you?

241
00:12:10,263 --> 00:12:11,720
他们当中有一个人杀了托尼
One of them killed Tony,

242
00:12:11,720 --> 00:12:13,640
我只是不知道是谁
I just don't know who.

243
00:12:13,640 --> 00:12:14,940
所以我就联系你了
That's why I called you.

244
00:12:14,940 --> 00:12:16,436
我需要你在条子赶来之前
I need you to solve this

245
00:12:16,436 --> 00:12:17,420
解决这个案子
before the cops show up.

246
00:12:17,420 --> 00:12:19,420
不然他们就会把我们所有人都抓起来
They will arrest every one of us

247
00:12:19,420 --> 00:12:21,060
只是为了把故事卖给那些八卦小报 
just to sell the story to the gossip rags, 

248
00:12:21,060 --> 00:12:22,520
接着转眼间 你还没反应过来呢
and then, poof, before you know it,

249
00:12:22,520 --> 00:12:24,111
我一半的客户都被炒鱿鱼了
half my clients, out of a job.

250
00:12:24,111 --> 00:12:25,840
所以我要保护好你的客户
So, protect your clients.

251
00:12:25,840 --> 00:12:28,260
当然啦 除了凶手
Except the murderer, obviously.

252
00:12:28,260 --> 00:12:29,540
我要跟那家伙解约
I'm going to drop them.

253
00:12:30,060 --> 00:12:31,985
尸体在哪里
Where's the body?

254
00:12:35,760 --> 00:12:37,060
在这里
In there.

255
00:12:37,534 --> 00:12:38,859
说实话
Staying honest,

256
00:12:38,859 --> 00:12:40,540
我几乎不敢看他
I could barely look at him.

257
00:12:41,080 --> 00:12:43,180
我会在客厅里拖住其他人
I'll stall the others in the sitting room

258
00:12:43,180 --> 00:12:46,700
你尽管去做你该做的事
while you go do what it is you... do.

259
00:12:47,440 --> 00:12:48,140
有火吗
Got a light?

260
00:12:49,780 --> 00:12:51,015
真棒
Fantastic.

261
00:12:51,860 --> 00:12:54,120
加州 好莱坞
Hollywood, California.

262
00:12:54,120 --> 00:12:56,260
豪宅 影星
Mansions, movie stars,

263
00:12:56,260 --> 00:12:57,777
和命案
and murder.

264
00:12:59,312 --> 00:13:00,981
窒息性死亡
Strangulation.

265
00:13:01,700 --> 00:13:02,782
但凶器是什么
But with what?

266
00:13:02,782 --> 00:13:04,200
在今晚九点钟
At 9:00 p.m. tonight,

267
00:13:04,200 --> 00:13:05,800
托尼·哈特
Tony Hart,

268
00:13:05,800 --> 00:13:07,960
洛蒙德电影制片厂负责人
head of Lomond Picture Studios

269
00:13:07,960 --> 00:13:09,460
在家中被人勒死
was strangled in his own home.

270
00:13:10,020 --> 00:13:11,658
然而凶器未知
But with what?

271
00:13:11,658 --> 00:13:13,160
凶手未知
And by whom?

272
00:13:13,160 --> 00:13:15,260
千万别忘了还要查清动机
And don't forget about the "why."

273
00:13:16,480 --> 00:13:17,400
找到杀人动机
Find your motive,

274
00:13:17,400 --> 00:13:18,498
你就能找到凶手
and you've got your killer.

275
00:13:18,498 --> 00:13:20,080
一般来说 动机都悄悄地
Usually, a motive hides

276
00:13:20,080 --> 00:13:21,734
藏在阴影之下
quiet secrets hidden in shadows

277
00:13:21,734 --> 00:13:23,403
藏在紧闭的门后
and behind closed doors,

278
00:13:23,403 --> 00:13:25,839
但我能看出这案子的要素十分齐全
but I could see this case had it all.

279
00:13:25,839 --> 00:13:28,280
激情 绝望
Passion, desperation,

280
00:13:28,280 --> 00:13:30,180
嫉妒 暴怒
jealousy, rage.

281
00:13:30,180 --> 00:13:32,920
至于这些嫌疑犯嘛
And as for the suspects,

282
00:13:32,920 --> 00:13:34,600
有些人你估计看着还眼熟
you may recognize some of the guests 

283
00:13:34,600 --> 00:13:37,260
洛蒙德电视台的太空冒险时间档
from Lomond's television space adventure hour,

284
00:13:37,680 --> 00:13:40,400
《星际边疆》的组员
The Last Frontier,

285
00:13:40,400 --> 00:13:42,990
例如该节目的主创 TK·贝洛斯
including the show's creator TK Bellows

286
00:13:42,990 --> 00:13:46,326
以及曾是演员 后来成为制片人的 桑尼·卢皮诺
and former actress turned producer Sunny Lupino.

287
00:13:46,326 --> 00:13:48,480
该剧的大明星 阿德莱德·肖
The show's stars-- Adelaide Shaw,

288
00:13:48,480 --> 00:13:51,980
麦克斯韦·圣和李·伍兹也在这里
Maxwell Saint and Lee Woods-- are also here,

289
00:13:51,980 --> 00:13:55,100
还有肖的心头肉 安东尼·麦克比奥
along with Shaw's main squeeze, Anthony MacBeau.

290
00:13:55,100 --> 00:13:57,837
而你已经见过顶级经纪人乔尼·格洛斯了
And you already met power agent Joni Gloss.

291
00:13:58,605 --> 00:14:01,760
这场聚会的东家 托尼·哈特死了
Your host, Tony Hart, is dead,

292
00:14:01,760 --> 00:14:03,676
而凶手就是你们之中的某人
and one of you murdered him.

293
00:14:08,520 --> 00:14:09,560
先别急 等一下
Hold your horses.

294
00:14:09,560 --> 00:14:12,280
我们这里为什么会有人想谋杀哈特
Why would one of us want to murder Hart?

295
00:14:12,280 --> 00:14:14,260
因为你的节目就要被砍了
Because your show was about to be canceled.

296
00:14:15,220 --> 00:14:17,060
开玩笑 我们可是大热门啊
Canceled? But we're a hit.

297
00:14:19,526 --> 00:14:22,229
哦 收视率
Oh. Ratings.

298
00:14:23,163 --> 00:14:25,500
好了 接下来
Now, here's how this is going to go.

299
00:14:25,500 --> 00:14:27,360
任何人都不许从那扇门出去
No one is gonna walk out of that door

300
00:14:27,360 --> 00:14:30,040
也不能打电话
or make any phone calls.

301
00:14:30,040 --> 00:14:31,360
你也不行 威廉·莫里斯
Even you, William Morris.

302
00:14:32,172 --> 00:14:33,780
我们得好好待在一起
We're all gonna get real cozy

303
00:14:33,780 --> 00:14:35,660
直到把这一切都弄清楚
until we've worked this all out.

304
00:14:35,660 --> 00:14:37,260
这种事不该发生在我头上啊
This can't be happening. To me.

305
00:14:37,740 --> 00:14:39,300
目前已知的信息有
What we know:

306
00:14:39,300 --> 00:14:41,860
今晚九点 有人用不明武器
At 9:00 p.m. tonight, someone strangled Tony Hart

307
00:14:41,860 --> 00:14:43,580
在卧室中勒死了托尼·哈特
with an unknown weapon in his bedroom.

308
00:14:43,960 --> 00:14:45,600
我们知道凶手就在这个房间里
We know the killer is in this room,

309
00:14:45,600 --> 00:14:48,760
而且我们知道 动机很可能是因为
and we know the likely motive is the cancelation

310
00:14:48,760 --> 00:14:50,423
《星际边疆》要被砍了
of The Last Frontier.

311
00:14:52,540 --> 00:14:55,080
而解开这个谜题的关键
And the key to this puzzle...

312
00:14:55,080 --> 00:14:57,697
像玻璃般清晰明了
...is as clear as glass.

313
00:15:03,320 --> 00:15:04,240
什么
What?

314
00:15:05,380 --> 00:15:07,880
等等 不是 不是我干的
Wait, it wasn't... it wasn't me.

315
00:15:07,880 --> 00:15:10,520
大家都知道你喝的是什么 朋友
Everyone knows your drink, pal.

316
00:15:10,920 --> 00:15:12,179
我相信你
I believe you.

317
00:15:12,179 --> 00:15:14,560
此外 你更喜欢偏冷色调的粉色
Besides, you favor a frostier shade of pink.

318
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:17,450
但这款色可是经典的
But this shade is classic.

319
00:15:17,450 --> 00:15:19,220
蜜丝佛陀的红宝石红
Max Factor's Ruby Red,

320
00:15:19,220 --> 00:15:21,260
1955年发售 并在各大
released in 1955, and splashed

321
00:15:21,260 --> 00:15:22,760
时尚杂志上大肆宣传
all over fashion magazines

322
00:15:22,760 --> 00:15:26,480
就涂在这位模特兼流行歌星标志性的嘴唇上
on the iconic face of model and pop star

323
00:15:26,480 --> 00:15:28,920
正是桑尼·卢皮诺
Sunny Lupino.

324
00:15:28,920 --> 00:15:30,580
不然呢 我可是引领潮流的巨星
What can I say, I'm a trendsetter.

325
00:15:31,480 --> 00:15:33,140
但这证明不了我就是凶手
But that doesn't make me a killer.

326
00:15:35,560 --> 00:15:36,936
确实不行
That doesn't.

327
00:15:37,680 --> 00:15:39,639
但这个可以
But this does.

328
00:15:41,623 --> 00:15:44,560
《星际边疆》是你身为制片人出品的第一个项目
The Last Frontier was your first project as a producer.

329
00:15:44,560 --> 00:15:46,040
你拼命争取让它成功播出
You fought to get it on the air,

330
00:15:46,040 --> 00:15:47,380
从你跟工作室的关系 到你的前夫 
leveraged your relationships with the studio

331
00:15:47,380 --> 00:15:48,948
全都是大好的资源
and your ex-husband.

332
00:15:49,499 --> 00:15:50,900
你把你的整个职业生涯都押上去了
Bet your whole career on it.

333
00:15:50,900 --> 00:15:52,880
托尼和我是离婚了 
Tony and I were divorced,

334
00:15:52,880 --> 00:15:55,740
但我们在工作方面一直都是互利互助
 but we were still very much invested in each other's success.

335
00:15:56,140 --> 00:15:58,460
你的投入比绝大多数人都多 不是吗
You were a little more invested than most, weren't you?

336
00:15:58,460 --> 00:16:02,040
想把太空剧带进美国家庭的客厅可是很烧钱的 所以
It's expensive to bring space into American living rooms, so

337
00:16:02,040 --> 00:16:04,564
你私下借了笔贷款
you took a personal loan from...

338
00:16:06,040 --> 00:16:08,320
借黑帮的钱 但要是剧被砍了的话
...the mob. But if the show was canceled,

339
00:16:08,320 --> 00:16:11,160
你就没法偿还这笔债务了 于是
you'd never be able to pay it back, so...

340
00:16:12,972 --> 00:16:15,460
你杀了托尼以求这部剧能继续播出
...you killed Tony to keep it on the air.

341
00:16:15,460 --> 00:16:18,440
关于此人我只知道一件事 他是我的粉丝
The only thing I know about that man is that he's a fan.

342
00:16:18,840 --> 00:16:20,240
来找我要签名的
He wanted an autograph.

343
00:16:20,980 --> 00:16:22,260
那又何必用长焦镜头呢
Why the telelens, then?

344
00:16:22,260 --> 00:16:25,560
我当时在佩里诺饭店跟约翰尼享用晚餐
I was having dinner at Perino's with Johnny.

345
00:16:25,560 --> 00:16:28,820
那人姓卡森 想让我参与一个全国广播公司的项目
Carson. He was trying to talk me into a project at NBC.

346
00:16:29,380 --> 00:16:31,060
托尼一直都在监视我
Tony was keeping tabs on me

347
00:16:31,060 --> 00:16:32,525
想确保我没有跟别人勾搭上
to make sure I wasn't being unfaithful.

348
00:16:33,020 --> 00:16:34,027
以防我想背后坑制片厂
To the studio.

349
00:16:34,900 --> 00:16:36,040
但你说对了
But you're right.

350
00:16:36,040 --> 00:16:37,180
我确实有做自己的投资
I did invest my own money,

351
00:16:37,180 --> 00:16:38,965
但钱不是从黑帮借来的
I just didn't take it from the mob.

352
00:16:39,320 --> 00:16:40,833
我把房子卖了
I sold the house.

353
00:16:41,380 --> 00:16:43,136
我和托尼的第一个房子
Mine and Tony's first house.

354
00:16:43,136 --> 00:16:44,780
啊 你不是可喜欢那间房子了吗
Oh, but you love that house.

355
00:16:44,780 --> 00:16:46,440
在说服艾尔弗雷德让我出演《乌鸦》之前
Until I convinced Alfred to put me in Crows, 

356
00:16:46,440 --> 00:16:48,600
 我还只是个无名小卒
I was just another pair of lips.

357
00:16:50,960 --> 00:16:52,320
但奥斯卡奖一到手 机会来了
But that Oscar opened doors.

358
00:16:52,320 --> 00:16:55,248
机会到手之后我干什么了 去买豪车吗
And what did I use it for, my own star vehicles?

359
00:16:55,248 --> 00:16:58,280
我没有 我听到TK在推销
No. When I heard TK's pitch

360
00:16:58,280 --> 00:17:00,140
他的《星际边疆》
for The Last Frontier,

361
00:17:00,660 --> 00:17:02,522
那一刻我就意识到 这部剧可不一般
I knew it was special.

362
00:17:02,522 --> 00:17:04,280
只要能拯救它 你做什么都愿意
And you'd do anything to save it.

363
00:17:04,280 --> 00:17:05,520
那不是废话
You're damn right, I would.

364
00:17:06,040 --> 00:17:07,500
我甚至找托尼商量我的计划
I even came to Tony with a plan.

365
00:17:07,500 --> 00:17:09,460
-但他拒绝了 -他同意了
- But he refused. - He agreed.

366
00:17:09,460 --> 00:17:10,700
我们还在商讨细节呢
We were going over the details

367
00:17:10,700 --> 00:17:12,080
结果聊了一半被麦克斯韦·圣打断了
when Maxwell Saint interrupted us.

368
00:17:12,600 --> 00:17:13,366
假如你真想知道
If you really want to know

369
00:17:13,366 --> 00:17:14,820
托尼到底怎么了
what happened to Tony,

370
00:17:14,820 --> 00:17:15,902
问他去
talk to him.

371
00:17:28,020 --> 00:17:29,040
天哪
Oh, my God.

372
00:17:32,420 --> 00:17:35,633
李 她死了吗
Lee? Is she dead?

373
00:17:35,633 --> 00:17:37,580
你知道我是个演员 不是医生吧
You know I'm an actor, not a doctor, right?

374
00:17:37,580 --> 00:17:39,080
但是你看她这模样
But, yeah. I mean, look at her.

375
00:17:39,080 --> 00:17:40,693
怎么看都是死了
She's obviously dead.

376
00:17:49,600 --> 00:17:50,770
死于中毒
Poison.

377
00:17:57,380 --> 00:17:58,340
斯考提 你在忙吗
Scotty, you busy?

378
00:17:58,340 --> 00:17:59,840
有点忙
A bit busy, yeah.

379
00:17:59,840 --> 00:18:03,160
你的模拟程序能耗有点超标 咋了
Your simulation is pulling a wee bit more power than expected. Why?

380
00:18:03,160 --> 00:18:05,220
以战斗模拟器为原型开发的全息甲板
Base a holodeck on a battle simulator

381
00:18:05,220 --> 00:18:06,440
反应也会和战斗模拟器一样
and it's going to act like one.

382
00:18:06,440 --> 00:18:07,200
什么意思
What does that mean?

383
00:18:07,200 --> 00:18:09,520
它看穿我了 预判了我的行动
Well, it's figured me out, learned my moves.

384
00:18:10,240 --> 00:18:11,740
好像真的是我的敌人一样
Just like an enemy opponent.

385
00:18:11,740 --> 00:18:13,080
这种设置怎么改
Well, how can I change that?

386
00:18:13,080 --> 00:18:14,160
不用改 我需要换个视角
No, I need a fresh eye,

387
00:18:14,160 --> 00:18:15,662
找一个和我思维不同的人来
someone who won't see things like I do.

388
00:18:16,120 --> 00:18:18,760
在第57本书《纸月旅馆谋杀案》里面
In book number 57, Murder at the Paper Moon Inn,

389
00:18:18,760 --> 00:18:20,460
艾米莉亚·穆恩找了一个搭档
Amelia Moon needed a partner.

390
00:18:20,460 --> 00:18:21,960
这个嘛 恐怕我帮不了你
Well, I'm afraid it can't be me

391
00:18:21,960 --> 00:18:23,760
没了我进取号要停摆的
if you want the Enterprise to continue running.

392
00:18:24,380 --> 00:18:26,139
噢 没事
Oh, no, that's okay.

393
00:18:27,660 --> 00:18:30,095
我觉得我已经有个完美的舞伴了
I think I might have the perfect dance partner already.

394
00:18:32,578 --> 00:18:34,460
史波克  多谢你来帮我
Spock, thank you for coming.

395
00:18:35,414 --> 00:18:37,083
我会尽力给你提供全面的帮助
I'm here to assist in any way I can.

396
00:18:37,083 --> 00:18:38,360
不过 我有一事想问
Though, may I ask,

397
00:18:38,360 --> 00:18:40,040
既然你已经输给了全息甲板的程序
if the holodeck has defeated you,

398
00:18:40,040 --> 00:18:41,240
为何不直接结束任务呢
why not just end the mission?

399
00:18:41,880 --> 00:18:44,180
听着 派克舰长给了我很明确的命令
Look, Pike gave me very clear orders:

400
00:18:44,180 --> 00:18:46,900
要用严苛的条件来测试这个设备
Test the device under rigorous circumstances.

401
00:18:46,900 --> 00:18:48,520
以及 我还没输呢 是我升级了
Also, it didn't defeat me, I leveled up

402
00:18:48,520 --> 00:18:49,629
然后它提高了难度
and then it increased the difficulty.

403
00:18:50,720 --> 00:18:51,740
再说了
Besides,

404
00:18:51,740 --> 00:18:54,080
艾米莉亚·穆恩在抓到凶手前绝不放弃
Amelia Moon doesn't give up until she gets her man,

405
00:18:54,080 --> 00:18:55,302
我也一样
and neither do I.

406
00:18:55,302 --> 00:18:57,220
我已经大致了解了案件
I have briefed myself on the case.

407
00:18:57,220 --> 00:18:59,172
侦探穆恩的搭档是什么样的
What was Detective Moon's partner like?

408
00:18:59,172 --> 00:19:00,320
想来应当是个好手
Proficient, I assume?

409
00:19:00,320 --> 00:19:01,460
他是个笨手笨脚的傻子
He was a bumbling idiot.

410
00:19:01,460 --> 00:19:03,320
-听起来没什么用处 -确实
- That does not seem useful. - No.

411
00:19:03,320 --> 00:19:04,844
但你的用处可大多了
You will be much more so.

412
00:19:05,740 --> 00:19:07,080
这是谁啊
Who's this guy?

413
00:19:07,080 --> 00:19:08,440
史波克侦探
Detective Spock.

414
00:19:08,440 --> 00:19:10,040
我的同事
He works with me.

415
00:19:10,040 --> 00:19:11,384
他怎么穿得跟来参加睡衣派对一样
I didn't know this was a pajama party.

416
00:19:11,384 --> 00:19:12,552
等等
Hang on.

417
00:19:13,360 --> 00:19:15,920
是演员分配部派你来的吗
Did Central Casting send you?

418
00:19:15,920 --> 00:19:16,789
就他那耳朵 开玩笑的吧
What, with those ears?

419
00:19:16,789 --> 00:19:18,620
史波克侦探不看电视
Detective Spock doesn't watch television.

420
00:19:18,620 --> 00:19:19,920
合着这哥们是共产党吗
So he's a communist?

421
00:19:20,800 --> 00:19:23,280
更像那种爱看电影的文艺逼
More likely one of those cinema snobs.

422
00:19:23,280 --> 00:19:24,820
这有什么关系
What does it matter?

423
00:19:25,980 --> 00:19:28,401
全息柯克似乎情绪很激动
The holo-Kirk seems particularly agitated.

424
00:19:29,040 --> 00:19:31,738
正常 他可是我的头号嫌犯
He should, he's number one on my suspect list.

425
00:19:32,940 --> 00:19:34,620
辛苦你赶过来了
Thanks for coming so fast.

426
00:19:34,620 --> 00:19:37,020
看看这些波动
These fluctuations... here.

427
00:19:37,020 --> 00:19:38,520
它们变得越发频繁了
They're becoming more frequent.

428
00:19:38,520 --> 00:19:40,360
考虑到那颗坍塌中的中子星只有六小时航程远
We are six hours from a collapsing star.

429
00:19:40,360 --> 00:19:42,480
有一些小波动是正常的
Minor surges are to be expected.

430
00:19:42,480 --> 00:19:43,750
大家全在通宵工作
Everyone's pulling an all-nighter.

431
00:19:43,750 --> 00:19:45,820
我甚至跟派克建议让奥特加斯复职
I even recommended Pike reinstate Ortegas.

432
00:19:45,820 --> 00:19:47,040
你信任她吗
And you trust her?

433
00:19:47,420 --> 00:19:48,060
当然
I do.

434
00:19:48,060 --> 00:19:50,890
辅助能源貌似也出现了些问题
Auxiliary power also seems to be having issues.

435
00:19:52,559 --> 00:19:54,794
这应该不在标准情况之下了
This seems beyond standard.

436
00:19:57,420 --> 00:19:59,497
别担心 一切都在掌控之中
Don't worry, I've got everything under control.

437
00:19:57,420 --> 00:19:59,497
传感器严重过载 电容电力故障 全息二极管分析中

438
00:19:59,497 --> 00:20:01,620
哇 这传感器过载得太夸张了吧
Wow, that is a sensory overload.

439
00:20:01,620 --> 00:20:03,920
噢都是正常的 都在掌控之中
Oh, all normal, all under control.

440
00:20:03,920 --> 00:20:06,900
全向全息二极管产生的变量
The omnidirectional holo-diodes produce

441
00:20:06,900 --> 00:20:09,776
实在是太多了 不太好全都关照到
a tremendous number of variables to keep an eye on.

442
00:20:10,720 --> 00:20:12,740
需要找个人帮你吗
Do you need a second set of eyes?

443
00:20:12,740 --> 00:20:13,913
没事 我能搞定
No, I've got it.

444
00:20:13,913 --> 00:20:16,383
以我的经验看 有时候多一个人
In my experience, sometimes a second set of eyes

445
00:20:16,383 --> 00:20:19,360
可能会适得其反 我能搞定的
can be... detrimental. I-I can handle it.

446
00:20:20,200 --> 00:20:22,540
好的 但我需要先签收你的工程日志
Okay, but I do need to sign off on your engineering logs

447
00:20:22,540 --> 00:20:24,260
然后再回去处理中子星的事
before returning to work on the neutron star.

448
00:20:24,260 --> 00:20:27,059
祝你能够打破之前那位总管留下的
Fingers crossed you improve upon the haphazard example

449
00:20:27,059 --> 00:20:29,280
一团乱麻的先例
set by your... supervisor.

450
00:20:29,280 --> 00:20:31,740
是的 我知道佩利亚的日志实在是
Yes, I'm familiar with, uh,

451
00:20:31,740 --> 00:20:33,740
臭名昭著
Pelia's infamous logs.

452
00:20:33,740 --> 00:20:36,035
老鹰都能把眼睛看瞎
An eagle could go blind from reading them.

453
00:20:38,940 --> 00:20:40,360
-这就撑不住了吗 -没有没有
- Broken already? - Oh, no, no.

454
00:20:40,360 --> 00:20:41,980
小毛病 在测试阶段很正常
Just a wee bug, to be expected with

455
00:20:41,980 --> 00:20:43,410
不用大惊小怪
beta phase testing.

456
00:20:43,410 --> 00:20:45,440
这模拟器毕竟这么大 它会自动调取
You know, a simulator this big will automatically pull

457
00:20:45,440 --> 00:20:48,014
算力来进行补偿 你明白的
processing power to compensate, but, you know,

458
00:20:48,014 --> 00:20:49,140
这算不上啥问题
it's not a problem.

459
00:20:49,680 --> 00:20:53,820
只要转移一些能量 没事啦
I'll just, um, divert a little juice. Yeah.

460
00:20:54,140 --> 00:20:55,755
虽说拉安是在实地亲力亲为的那个
La'An may be running this test,

461
00:20:55,755 --> 00:20:57,624
不过
but, uh,

462
00:20:57,624 --> 00:20:59,492
坚强的后盾可是你啊
you're the failsafe.

463
00:21:03,060 --> 00:21:04,464
明白明白
Understood. Loud and clear.

464
00:21:04,464 --> 00:21:05,798
我一定能搞定哒
But, you know, I've got it.

465
00:21:10,236 --> 00:21:13,940
圣先生 是你杀了托尼·哈特和桑尼·卢皮诺吗
Mr. Saint, did you kill Tony Hart and Sunny Lupino?

466
00:21:14,511 --> 00:21:15,880
不是
Nope.

467
00:21:15,880 --> 00:21:16,940
是你吗
Did you?

468
00:21:16,940 --> 00:21:18,200
桑尼说 托尼死之前
Sonny said you and Tony

469
00:21:18,200 --> 00:21:20,140
你和他在吵架
were fighting before he died.

470
00:21:20,140 --> 00:21:22,349
小打小闹罢了
A tiff. A row.

471
00:21:22,349 --> 00:21:24,016
退一万步说 吵了两句吧
A tangle, maybe.

472
00:21:24,016 --> 00:21:25,540
没啥好搬出来讲的
It's not even worth discussing.

473
00:21:28,522 --> 00:21:29,656
不过是因为有人嫉妒了
It was jealousy.

474
00:21:29,656 --> 00:21:30,890
嫉妒
Jealousy?

475
00:21:33,380 --> 00:21:34,661
你的手镯
Your cuff.

476
00:21:34,661 --> 00:21:36,863
在作案现场有一个一模一样的
There was an identical one at the crime scene.

477
00:21:38,200 --> 00:21:41,834
这是哈特的秘书送我的廉价小玩意
A little trinket from Hart's secretary.

478
00:21:43,026 --> 00:21:43,860
她喜欢我
She likes me.

479
00:21:43,860 --> 00:21:45,572
你们在搞外遇
You were having an affair.

480
00:21:46,900 --> 00:21:48,007
被你发现了
You caught me.

481
00:21:48,007 --> 00:21:49,509
哈特先生对此有意见 是吧
And Mr. Hart had an issue with this?

482
00:21:49,509 --> 00:21:53,012
刚巧只是因为他在和同一位秘书搞外遇啦
Well, only because he was having an affair with the same secretary.

483
00:21:53,440 --> 00:21:54,347
听起来很复杂
sounds complicated.

484
00:21:54,347 --> 00:21:55,800
并没有 随便玩玩罢了
No, not really. It was casual.

485
00:21:56,360 --> 00:21:57,984
人与人之间一旦开始紧密合作
You work closely with people,

486
00:21:57,984 --> 00:21:59,819
奇妙的事情自然会发生
and things happen.

487
00:22:07,660 --> 00:22:09,896
想必二位一定深有感触
You two must know how that goes.

488
00:22:09,896 --> 00:22:11,330
什么 我们
What? We--

489
00:22:12,298 --> 00:22:14,534
没有 这是你的事
No, this-this is about you,

490
00:22:14,534 --> 00:22:16,440
与别人无关
not... anyone else.

491
00:22:16,440 --> 00:22:18,340
听着 我是一个演员
Look, I'm an actor.

492
00:22:18,340 --> 00:22:19,400
我喜欢演戏
I like drama,

493
00:22:19,400 --> 00:22:21,940
但绝对没必要出于这种理由杀人
but it's certainly nothing to kill for.

494
00:22:21,940 --> 00:22:23,543
另外 我早骗过了哈特
And besides, I had already convinced Hart that

495
00:22:23,543 --> 00:22:25,760
跟他说我与那位秘书分手了
it was over between me and the secretary.

496
00:22:25,760 --> 00:22:27,113
他怎么就信你了
And how did you do that?

497
00:22:28,460 --> 00:22:29,700
我和麦克斯韦鬼混吗
Me and Maxwell?

498
00:22:29,700 --> 00:22:32,140
绝对百分百没门
Absolutely 100% never.

499
00:22:32,140 --> 00:22:33,700
你好像情绪很激动啊
You seem awfully heated about that.

500
00:22:33,700 --> 00:22:36,440
他是个极端大男子主义的自大狂
He's a chauvinistic egomaniac.

501
00:22:37,300 --> 00:22:39,840
光是跟他待在同一个布景里我都忍不了
I can barely stand to be on set with the guy.

502
00:22:39,840 --> 00:22:41,880
我跟他上床图啥啊
Why would I go to bed with him?

503
00:22:41,880 --> 00:22:43,730
你知不知道这部剧要被砍了
Were you aware that the show was being cancelled?

504
00:22:44,597 --> 00:22:45,698
知道些小道消息
I heard whispers.

505
00:22:46,180 --> 00:22:47,434
你对此有什么想法
How did you feel about it?

506
00:22:47,434 --> 00:22:49,360
这个嘛
Well,

507
00:22:49,360 --> 00:22:50,703
我的台词和裙子
my lines and my skirts have been

508
00:22:50,703 --> 00:22:53,060
越往后拍越短
getting shorter and shorter with every episode,

509
00:22:53,140 --> 00:22:54,800
唯一一个
and the only person

510
00:22:54,800 --> 00:22:57,600
为我的角色争取权利的就是桑尼
who ever fought for my character was Sunny.

511
00:22:57,600 --> 00:23:00,279
现在她也死了
And now she's dead, so...

512
00:23:02,200 --> 00:23:04,160
你知道我在西区出演海达·高布乐时
Did you know that I was just 18 when I played

513
00:23:04,160 --> 00:23:05,989
才十八岁吗
Hedda Gabler on the West End?

514
00:23:06,920 --> 00:23:10,300
二位侦探 我是个好演员
I'm good at what I do, Detectives.

515
00:23:10,300 --> 00:23:12,600
但别人似乎只关心你的感情生活如何
But all anyone seems to care about is your love life.

516
00:23:13,620 --> 00:23:14,600
肯定很令人沮丧吧
Must be frustrating.

517
00:23:14,600 --> 00:23:16,840
是啊 很沮丧
Yeah, it is.

518
00:23:16,840 --> 00:23:19,080
我只是想要在职业生涯中
But is it wrong to want love

519
00:23:19,080 --> 00:23:21,233
兼顾爱情和我应得的尊重 这有什么错吗
and to be taken seriously in my career?

520
00:23:24,036 --> 00:23:26,080
那你觉得 为什么你和圣先生
So, why do you think there are persistent rumors

521
00:23:26,080 --> 00:23:27,807
之间的流言总是屡次三番地被提起呢
about your affair with Mr. Saint?

522
00:23:33,340 --> 00:23:34,980
你觉得卢皮诺小姐是个什么样的人
How did you feel about Miss Lupino?

523
00:23:34,980 --> 00:23:37,260
你是说 我有没有杀她的动机
You mean, did I have a reason to kill her?

524
00:23:38,150 --> 00:23:39,480
没有
No.

525
00:23:40,640 --> 00:23:41,960
我敬佩她
I admired her.

526
00:23:42,400 --> 00:23:45,858
她不愿意只做一个花瓶
She couldn't settle for being a work of art.

527
00:23:45,858 --> 00:23:48,680
她想要成为艺术的创作人
She wanted to make art.

528
00:23:48,680 --> 00:23:50,280
你对艺术很看重啊
Art means a lot to you.

529
00:23:50,280 --> 00:23:52,020
艺术就是一切
It's everything.

530
00:23:52,020 --> 00:23:54,980
如果说我想要赠给世人什么礼物
If I can give a gift to the world,

531
00:23:54,980 --> 00:23:56,600
那就是帮助人们解放
I want to help people unleash

532
00:23:56,600 --> 00:23:58,500
心中那头艺术的野兽
the artistic beast inside of them.

533
00:23:59,220 --> 00:24:02,360
怎么解放你这所谓的艺术野兽
How does one "unleash the artistic beast"?

534
00:24:02,360 --> 00:24:04,000
我一直在办一个艺术家沙龙
I've been doing an artists salon.

535
00:24:04,840 --> 00:24:06,740
李之前可能和你们讲过了
Lee probably told you about it.

536
00:24:06,740 --> 00:24:09,180
具体陈述一下沙龙的活动
What goes on at an artists salon?

537
00:24:09,180 --> 00:24:10,683
麦克弹吉他
Mac plays guitar.

538
00:24:10,683 --> 00:24:13,040
其他人有的唱歌 有的画画
Others sing, paint.

539
00:24:13,040 --> 00:24:14,160
你呢
And you?

540
00:24:14,160 --> 00:24:15,220
李写些东西
Lee writes.

541
00:24:15,220 --> 00:24:17,220
确切地说 她最近在写一部剧本
She's been writing a screenplay, actually.

542
00:24:17,220 --> 00:24:18,380
电影的剧本
A movie.

543
00:24:18,380 --> 00:24:19,360
什么剧本
A screenplay?

544
00:24:19,360 --> 00:24:20,425
怎么问起这个
Why?

545
00:24:20,425 --> 00:24:21,661
麦克跟你们说的吗
Mac told you that?

546
00:24:21,661 --> 00:24:25,097
在达科他州上演的一部西部片
A western set in the Dakotas.

547
00:24:25,097 --> 00:24:27,240
被害人房间里就有一本剧本
There was a script in the victim's room,

548
00:24:27,240 --> 00:24:28,080
写的是达科他州的故事
about the Dakotas.

549
00:24:29,600 --> 00:24:31,137
还有谁知道剧本的事
Who else knew about this?

550
00:24:36,780 --> 00:24:38,480
打算畏罪潜逃哈
Guilty conscience got you running?

551
00:24:38,480 --> 00:24:40,220
不是畏罪 是胃病
More like a weak stomach.

552
00:24:41,300 --> 00:24:43,583
多年心血付之东流
Must be hard to watch something you've poured so much into

553
00:24:43,583 --> 00:24:45,320
很难受吧
just disappear.

554
00:24:46,554 --> 00:24:48,480
心里确实是疙疙瘩瘩的
It's not my favorite feeling, no.

555
00:24:48,480 --> 00:24:51,120
是不是收视率太低了 不能续订第二季
But the ratings were too low to warrant a season two?

556
00:24:51,120 --> 00:24:54,680
粉丝虽然不多 但还是充满热情的嘛
Our fanbase is small, but it's quite passionate.

557
00:24:54,680 --> 00:24:55,695
伍兹小姐的西部电影
Were you threatened

558
00:24:55,695 --> 00:24:57,680
有没有让你感到受威胁
by the Western motion picture Miss Woods wrote?

559
00:24:57,680 --> 00:25:00,920
李又写了一部西部片吗 挺好的
Lee wrote another Western? Good for her.

560
00:25:01,480 --> 00:25:03,260
她就喜欢吊死在这种早过时了的题材上
She'll never tire of that dying genre.

561
00:25:03,260 --> 00:25:04,837
所以 你知道剧本的事
So, you knew about the script?

562
00:25:06,200 --> 00:25:07,280
不觉得嫉妒吗
You weren't jealous?

563
00:25:08,140 --> 00:25:09,480
谈谈电视剧被砍的事吧
What about the cancellation?

564
00:25:09,480 --> 00:25:10,460
这也是你之前就知道的吗
Did you know about that, too?

565
00:25:12,180 --> 00:25:14,581
于是你就撕合同了 冲冠一怒 是吗
Is that why you ripped up your contract? Out of anger?

566
00:25:16,800 --> 00:25:19,880
你知道他们是怎么评价第一季的吗
Do you know what they say about a show after its first season?

567
00:25:19,880 --> 00:25:21,860
不知道 说说看吧
No. What do they say?

568
00:25:21,860 --> 00:25:23,455
有一种没过脑子的美感
Practically writes itself.

569
00:25:25,380 --> 00:25:27,060
哈特撕的合同 不是我
Hart ripped up that contract, not me.

570
00:25:27,060 --> 00:25:28,420
真是帮了我个忙
He was actually doing me a favor.

571
00:25:28,420 --> 00:25:30,540
你早就想离开节目了吗
You wanted to leave the show?

572
00:25:30,540 --> 00:25:33,220
有本我中意已久的书 版权在华纳兄弟公司手里
Warners has the rights to a book I've been chasing.

573
00:25:33,220 --> 00:25:34,500
他们甚至同意让我来执导了
They're even gonna let me direct.

574
00:25:34,500 --> 00:25:37,880
是啊 我真心喜欢这部剧
Yeah, I-I-I love our show,

575
00:25:37,880 --> 00:25:39,505
但那可是电影啊
but movies...

576
00:25:40,160 --> 00:25:42,540
电影才能真正改造人的灵魂 孩子们
That's how you change hearts and minds, kids.

577
00:25:42,540 --> 00:25:44,600
这么说来 剧被砍了你还挺开心的
So, you're happy the show was being canceled?

578
00:25:44,600 --> 00:25:46,480
侦探大人
Oh, Detective.

579
00:25:47,320 --> 00:25:48,660
我是作家
I'm a writer.

580
00:25:48,660 --> 00:25:50,449
我对什么事都高兴不起来
I'm never happy about anything.

581
00:25:51,217 --> 00:25:52,852
但我没杀人
But I didn't kill anyone.

582
00:26:00,680 --> 00:26:02,061
他们身为同事
They all worked together,

583
00:26:02,061 --> 00:26:03,600
却任由私人情绪泛滥
yet allowed their emotions to jeopardize

584
00:26:03,600 --> 00:26:05,331
妨碍了共同的工作
the very work that they all shared.

585
00:26:10,500 --> 00:26:11,400
这是什么
What is that?

586
00:26:11,400 --> 00:26:13,680
李·伍兹的剧本
Lee Woods's script.

587
00:26:13,680 --> 00:26:15,280
我就知道有什么不对劲
I knew something was off about it.

588
00:26:15,280 --> 00:26:16,940
看 没封面
Look, no title page.

589
00:26:17,700 --> 00:26:18,745
为什么呢
But why?

590
00:26:20,120 --> 00:26:22,120
也许是为了隐去剧本的作者
Perhaps to hide the connection to the writer.

591
00:26:22,120 --> 00:26:24,516
不 不是贝洛斯干的 他不在乎这个
No, no, no, not from Bellows. He didn't even care.

592
00:26:25,840 --> 00:26:26,641
不对
No.

593
00:26:28,113 --> 00:26:30,589
有没有可能 不是李撕掉的
What if Lee's not the one who removed it?

594
00:26:30,589 --> 00:26:31,858
拉安
La'An...

595
00:26:35,705 --> 00:26:37,140
看起来吊灯是
The chandelier appears to have been

596
00:26:37,140 --> 00:26:38,474
被故意切断来伤害我们的
purposefully cut to harm us.

597
00:26:39,300 --> 00:26:40,499
为了阻止我们
To stop us

598
00:26:40,499 --> 00:26:42,034
因为我们已经靠近真相了
because we're close.

599
00:26:43,060 --> 00:26:45,060
剧本没有封面
The screenplay doesn't have a title page

600
00:26:45,540 --> 00:26:46,960
是因为剧本被人偷走了
because it was stolen.

601
00:26:46,960 --> 00:26:49,900
哈特偷了李的剧本 把作者改成其他人
Hart stole Lee's script and was going to credit someone else,

602
00:26:49,900 --> 00:26:52,244
也许是想归功给某个男的 那个年代常有这种事
probably a man, because that happened all the time back then.

603
00:26:53,720 --> 00:26:55,240
于是她就把哈特杀了
So she killed him for it.

604
00:27:02,520 --> 00:27:03,960
有更要紧的事
There is a more pressing matter.

605
00:27:05,880 --> 00:27:06,740
怎么有血
Blood?

606
00:27:07,100 --> 00:27:09,320
我记得全息甲板不是有有安全协议的吗
Well, I-I thought the holodeck had safety protocols.

607
00:27:10,080 --> 00:27:11,664
也许是出故障了
Perhaps they are malfunctioning.

608
00:27:13,540 --> 00:27:15,360
我们得离开这里 不要冒险
We should get out of here, not risk anything else.

609
00:27:16,200 --> 00:27:17,804
计算机 终止程序
Computer, end program.

610
00:27:21,200 --> 00:27:23,542
斯考特先生 把程序停下
Mr. Scott, please end program.

611
00:27:26,846 --> 00:27:28,715
计算机 显示拱门
Computer, arch.

612
00:27:31,300 --> 00:27:32,919
这下
So...

613
00:27:32,919 --> 00:27:34,460
我们关不掉它了
we can't shut it off,

614
00:27:35,220 --> 00:27:37,356
而且程序真的能伤害我们
the program could actually hurt us,

615
00:27:37,920 --> 00:27:39,240
我们还出不去
and we can't get out.

616
00:27:39,240 --> 00:27:40,659
正是如此
Indeed.

617
00:27:54,073 --> 00:27:56,560
斯考特中尉 你在找我吗
Lieutenant Scott, are you looking for me?

618
00:27:56,560 --> 00:28:00,100
这样 假设一下我们出了点通讯故障
Say I've got this hypothetical communications problem,

619
00:28:00,100 --> 00:28:02,820
你能不能给我点指导 像往常一样
could you advise me on this problem that, again,

620
00:28:02,820 --> 00:28:04,300
我是说假设哈 并不是真出了乱子
you know, it's not a real problem,

621
00:28:04,300 --> 00:28:06,860
你不要按字面意思理解这个词
in the traditional sense of the word "problem."

622
00:28:06,860 --> 00:28:08,700
我大概明白你的意思
I think I followed that.

623
00:28:08,700 --> 00:28:10,860
假设有一种非常小概率的事件发生了
In the highly unlikely event

624
00:28:10,860 --> 00:28:14,260
就是说呢 我和全息甲板里的拉安彻底失联了
that I were to have lost all contact with La'An inside the holodeck, 

625
00:28:14,260 --> 00:28:16,340
 你的建议是什么
what would you advise?

626
00:28:17,440 --> 00:28:19,100
如果失联的话
Well, if comms failed,

627
00:28:19,100 --> 00:28:20,980
我会绕过局部子处理器
I'd bypass local subprocessors

628
00:28:20,980 --> 00:28:22,840
直接联通光电数据网络
 and patch directly into the optical data network.

629
00:28:22,840 --> 00:28:25,460
好 我们再假设一下
Yeah. Imagine in this hypothetical,

630
00:28:25,460 --> 00:28:28,160
我已经这样尝试了若干次
like, I've already done that, multiple times.

631
00:28:28,160 --> 00:28:31,920
假设说来 我会去直接关闭模拟
Hypothetically, I'd shut the simulation down.

632
00:28:31,920 --> 00:28:33,940
现在看来 我估计你
Which, I'm assuming,

633
00:28:33,940 --> 00:28:35,940
在假设条件下 已经试过了
you've already, hypothetically, done.

634
00:28:35,940 --> 00:28:38,985
斯考提啊 你是说拉安被困在全息甲板里了吗
Scotty, are you telling me La'An is trapped in the holodeck?

635
00:28:40,553 --> 00:28:42,822
你要不试试 敲敲门
Have you tried knocking on the door?

636
00:28:42,822 --> 00:28:44,340
或者把门炸了
Or simply blowing it off?

637
00:28:44,340 --> 00:28:47,500
全息甲板里面的各类力场 牵引光束还有高精度二极管
The holodeck is a complex balance of forcefields, tractor beams, 

638
00:28:47,500 --> 00:28:49,800
之间的平衡极为复杂
and precision-guided diodes,

639
00:28:49,800 --> 00:28:50,562
而且设备全都直连主机
all hardwired in.

640
00:28:50,562 --> 00:28:52,920
所以炸门会瘫痪整个计算机系统
So, blowing it up would crash our entire computer system.

641
00:28:52,920 --> 00:28:55,020
修不好的那种 经过我的计算
Permanently. Per my calculations,

642
00:28:55,020 --> 00:28:56,940
除非拉安上尉走完程序的流程
the only way to unlock the program

643
00:28:56,940 --> 00:28:58,200
没有其他办法解除程序锁定
is for the lieutenant to complete it,

644
00:28:58,200 --> 00:28:58,938
但她完全不知情
but she's unaware of this.

645
00:28:58,938 --> 00:29:00,320
怎么样才能走完流程
What does completing it entail?

646
00:29:00,320 --> 00:29:02,641
破一桩一九六九年的好莱坞谋杀案
Solving a murder mystery set in 1969 Hollywood.

647
00:29:05,352 --> 00:29:06,920
我会帮你的
I'm on it.

648
00:29:06,920 --> 00:29:08,247
谢谢你 少尉
Thank you, Ensign.

649
00:29:08,247 --> 00:29:11,000
你知道这都不是假设吧
you-you know that wasn't all hypothetical?

650
00:29:11,000 --> 00:29:12,840
是啊 你刚开口我就知道了
Yeah, I caught on almost immediately.

651
00:29:12,840 --> 00:29:13,619
好的
Okay.

652
00:29:16,460 --> 00:29:18,757
很不幸 在模拟程序里
Unfortunately, I was unable to access the panel

653
00:29:18,757 --> 00:29:19,892
各面板无法响应
while in the simulation.

654
00:29:19,892 --> 00:29:22,200
我还是联络不上斯考特或是舰上的任何人
I still can't reach Scotty over comms or anyone on the ship.

655
00:29:22,200 --> 00:29:23,560
所以我们既有计算机问题
So, we have a computer problem

656
00:29:23,560 --> 00:29:24,630
又有通讯问题
and a communications problem.

657
00:29:24,630 --> 00:29:26,365
别忘了还有谋杀案
We also have a murderer problem.

658
00:29:26,365 --> 00:29:29,120
如果杀手要对我们动手 我们真的会死
If the killer comes after us, we could actually die in here.

659
00:29:29,120 --> 00:29:32,100
所以也许唯一的活路是抓出凶手
So maybe the only way to survive is to catch the murderer.

660
00:29:32,771 --> 00:29:34,060
也就是说
Which means...

661
00:29:35,107 --> 00:29:36,575
得把案子彻底破掉
we're going to go solve this mystery.

662
00:29:36,575 --> 00:29:37,810
我只是
I-I just...

663
00:29:37,944 --> 00:29:39,979
无法相信你想离开剧组
can't believe you wanted off the show.

664
00:29:40,260 --> 00:29:42,415
你不是也想离开吗
You also wanted off the show.

665
00:29:42,415 --> 00:29:44,484
你猜怎么着 我看你就是恨我
You know what I think? I think you hate me,

666
00:29:44,484 --> 00:29:46,953
还恨我给了你这辈子
and you hate the fact that I gave you the best job

667
00:29:46,953 --> 00:29:48,980
能接到的最好的工作
that you're ever gonna have.

668
00:29:48,980 --> 00:29:50,540
你在威胁我吗
Are you threatening me?

669
00:29:50,540 --> 00:29:51,790
都听见了吧
Did you all hear that?

670
00:29:51,790 --> 00:29:53,400
TK在威胁我
TK threatened me!

671
00:29:53,400 --> 00:29:54,840
他讲的是实话
He tells no lies.

672
00:29:54,840 --> 00:29:55,761
你又懂上了
What would you know?

673
00:29:55,761 --> 00:29:58,100
你只是给阿德莱德当跑路的下家的
You're only here as Adelaide's escape hatch.

674
00:29:58,100 --> 00:29:59,300
你这又什么意思呢
What is that supposed to mean?

675
00:29:59,300 --> 00:30:02,160
观众不喜欢你
Audiences don't like you.

676
00:30:02,160 --> 00:30:05,337
至少我懂怎么正常地念台词
At least I can deliver a line realistically.

677
00:30:05,337 --> 00:30:07,120
我那叫表演
It's called acting.

678
00:30:07,120 --> 00:30:08,700
你知道什么才是不正常的吗
And you know what's not realistic?

679
00:30:08,700 --> 00:30:09,680
一个女大副
 A lady first officer.

680
00:30:09,680 --> 00:30:11,978
承认现实吧 你早就明白自己没什么前途
Face it. You knew your days were limited.

681
00:30:11,978 --> 00:30:14,260
于是你才嫁了这个摇滚巨星
That's why you agreed to marry Mick Bowie over here,

682
00:30:14,260 --> 00:30:16,500
做他的小迷妹 跟着他演出就不显眼了
so you could disappear on tour as his groupie

683
00:30:16,500 --> 00:30:18,320
就没人会注意到你的职业生涯早完蛋了
and nobody would notice that your career was dead!

684
00:30:18,320 --> 00:30:21,720
你们都给我闭嘴
Everyone shut up, now!

685
00:30:22,920 --> 00:30:24,180
好了
Right.

686
00:30:24,180 --> 00:30:26,558
李·伍兹去哪儿了
Where is Lee Woods?

687
00:30:27,480 --> 00:30:30,796
这个睡衣男到底是哪儿冒出来的
And who is this guy?

688
00:30:34,400 --> 00:30:36,120
她死了
She's dead.

689
00:30:37,040 --> 00:30:38,208
乔尼·格洛斯
Joni Gloss.

690
00:30:38,208 --> 00:30:40,180
不是这样的 你误会了
It's not what it looks like.

691
00:30:40,180 --> 00:30:41,640
我只想是来借个火
I was just looking for a light.

692
00:30:41,640 --> 00:30:42,880
我找到她时她就已经死了
She was dead when I found her.

693
00:30:42,880 --> 00:30:44,620
星际边疆这部剧要是被砍
You had quite a bit of cash to lose

694
00:30:44,620 --> 00:30:46,400
你的经济损失应该会不小吧
from the cancelation of The Last Frontier, didn't you?

695
00:30:46,400 --> 00:30:48,740
我在节目里有三个客户 你算算损失大不大
I had three clients on that show. You do the math.

696
00:30:48,740 --> 00:30:51,060
但我没杀托尼·哈特
But I didn't kill Tony Hart,

697
00:30:51,060 --> 00:30:52,480
虽说我恨不得杀了他
though I wish I had.

698
00:30:52,480 --> 00:30:53,752
为什么
And why is that?

699
00:30:55,165 --> 00:30:56,600
因为砍掉《星际边疆》
Because canceling The Last Frontier

700
00:30:56,600 --> 00:30:58,540
是托尼做过的最蠢的事
is the stupidest thing Tony's ever done.

701
00:30:58,540 --> 00:31:01,727
你知道这样的一部剧有多难得吗
Do you realize how rare a show like this is?

702
00:31:01,727 --> 00:31:04,740
TK想要做的是通过科幻世界
TK wanted to give audiences a digestible reflection

703
00:31:04,740 --> 00:31:08,300
来给观众们呈现他们能看懂的 关于现实世界的反思
of their own world through the lens of fantasy.

704
00:31:08,300 --> 00:31:10,680
通过外星人的橡胶头套与故事情节中的隐喻
Social commentary with rubber masks

705
00:31:10,680 --> 00:31:14,100
给出社会评论 科幻嘛 就是这样的
and buried metaphors. You know, science fiction.

706
00:31:14,100 --> 00:31:16,120
公司反对他的远大图景 是吗
And the studio did not agree with this vision?

707
00:31:17,080 --> 00:31:19,078
他们更倾向于
They were more...

708
00:31:19,078 --> 00:31:20,720
谨言慎行
cautious.

709
00:31:20,720 --> 00:31:23,420
不愿意在社会上掀起波澜 这帮懦夫
Didn't want to "make waves." The cowards.

710
00:31:23,420 --> 00:31:26,020
TK希望星际边疆能取代这个腐烂的世界
TK wanted Frontier to take our rotten world,

711
00:31:26,020 --> 00:31:28,560
远离蝇营狗苟 不仁不义
with its warts and injustices,

712
00:31:28,560 --> 00:31:30,640
给观众一些更美好的东西
and give audiences something better.

713
00:31:30,640 --> 00:31:33,460
这么多高大上的 就凭这每周一集的太空冒险故事?
And all of that with weekly space adventures?

714
00:31:33,460 --> 00:31:36,280
你不觉得这个理念很鼓舞人心吗
You don't find the idea inspiring?

715
00:31:36,280 --> 00:31:39,120
你不觉得看到这部剧的孩子们也许会
You don't think some kid out there is going to see this show

716
00:31:39,120 --> 00:31:41,440
尽其余生仰观宇宙之大 探索星辰大海吗
and spend the rest of their life searching the stars?

717
00:31:41,960 --> 00:31:44,560
你不觉得对一个人来说
You don't think a person can love a piece of art

718
00:31:44,560 --> 00:31:46,680
所深爱的艺术 又或是音乐或故事
or music or a story so much

719
00:31:46,680 --> 00:31:48,760
都能够治愈心灵吗
that it heals them?

720
00:31:48,760 --> 00:31:52,360
通过展现人们从未知晓的一部分自己
Shows them parts of themselves they'd never even seen before?

721
00:31:52,360 --> 00:31:53,360
他们不会觉得看到了希望吗
And give them hope?

722
00:31:55,800 --> 00:31:57,720
呃 是这个道理
Well, no, of-of course I do.

723
00:31:57,720 --> 00:32:00,060
像这样的作品就不该有完结的一天
A show like this could've gone on forever.

724
00:32:00,060 --> 00:32:01,440
它能让一代又一代的粉丝知道
Given generations

725
00:32:01,440 --> 00:32:03,800
在这里 他们能够被看见 感受到归属感
of fans a place to feel seen, to belong,

726
00:32:04,440 --> 00:32:06,720
让他们能敢于重新拾起信仰
something to believe in again,

727
00:32:06,720 --> 00:32:09,328
无论他们是谁 来自什么地方
no matter who they were or where they came from.

728
00:32:10,529 --> 00:32:14,766
但要是没有第二季 这一切都是空谈
But you can't do any of that without a season two.

729
00:32:18,470 --> 00:32:21,140
终于给我找到火了
Finally, a light.

730
00:32:21,140 --> 00:32:23,675
假壁炉
A fake fire?

731
00:32:24,660 --> 00:32:26,220
托尼对电影的品味无可挑剔
Tony had impeccable taste in film,

732
00:32:26,220 --> 00:32:27,813
但他对装饰的品味真是没救了
but his sense of decor is just tragic.

733
00:32:27,813 --> 00:32:29,640
壁炉里是什么
What's inside the fireplace?

734
00:32:34,946 --> 00:32:36,380
赛璐珞胶片
Celluloid film.

735
00:32:36,380 --> 00:32:38,440
在22世纪就停用了
Discontinued in the 22nd century,

736
00:32:38,440 --> 00:32:40,540
许多人说这是电影行业的损失
many say to the detriment of cinema.

737
00:32:40,540 --> 00:32:41,860
我想这就是杀人凶器
I think this is the murder weapon.

738
00:32:46,520 --> 00:32:48,640
但同时也是一份记录的载体
But it's also a recording.

739
00:32:52,360 --> 00:32:55,320
这胶片里录有杀手想销毁的东西
There's something on this film the killer wanted to destroy,

740
00:32:55,320 --> 00:32:57,509
但他和乔尼一样看错了这片壁炉
but made the same mistake Joni did.

741
00:32:58,880 --> 00:33:00,600
史波克 我们必须看看这里面有什么
Spock, we have to see what's on this.

742
00:33:00,600 --> 00:33:02,860
好吧 中子星马上要坍塌了
All right, neutron star collapse is imminent.

743
00:33:02,860 --> 00:33:04,780
乌乎拉 扫描仪在收集数据了吗
Uhura, are scanners receiving data?

744
00:33:04,780 --> 00:33:05,717
正好收到 舰长
Right on time, sir.

745
00:33:06,831 --> 00:33:08,500
舰长 我监测到一片伽玛射线爆发
Captain, I'm detecting a gamma burst

746
00:33:08,500 --> 00:33:10,500
正冲向我们的航行路线
heading into our flight path.

747
00:33:10,500 --> 00:33:12,260
它的能量强度超乎预料地高
It's heavier energy than expected.

748
00:33:12,260 --> 00:33:13,559
传感器已经过载
The sensors are overloading.

749
00:33:16,480 --> 00:33:17,540
升起护盾
Shields up.

750
00:33:17,540 --> 00:33:18,440
打开黄色警报
Let's go to yellow alert.

751
00:33:18,440 --> 00:33:19,540
奥特加斯 带我们下去
Ortegas, take us down.

752
00:33:19,540 --> 00:33:20,500
尽可能绕开它
Steer as clear as you can.

753
00:33:20,500 --> 00:33:21,260
我也想
I'd like to,

754
00:33:21,260 --> 00:33:23,620
但能量刚刚忽然被消耗了一大截
but we just had a massive power drain.

755
00:33:23,620 --> 00:33:24,820
引擎无响应了
Engines aren't responding.

756
00:33:24,820 --> 00:33:26,660
护盾也是
Neither are shields.

757
00:33:26,660 --> 00:33:28,420
舰桥呼叫科学实验室
Bridge to Science Lab.

758
00:33:28,420 --> 00:33:29,740
斯科特先生 我们的系统怎么了
Mr. Scott, what's happening to our system?

759
00:33:29,740 --> 00:33:31,720
好吧 看起来全息甲板的能耗
Well, it seems the holodeck

760
00:33:31,720 --> 00:33:34,460
还是比我预料的要多一点点
is pulling a wee bit more power than I'd anticipated.

761
00:33:34,460 --> 00:33:35,580
那就把它关了
Then shut it down.

762
00:33:35,580 --> 00:33:37,649
舰桥有情况 我现在就需要能量
We have a situation on the bridge, and I need power, now.

763
00:33:37,649 --> 00:33:40,000
好的 但这事很复杂 舰长
Yeah, it's not quite that easy, sir.

764
00:33:40,000 --> 00:33:40,860
红色警报
Red alert.

765
00:33:41,960 --> 00:33:43,260
斯科特先生
Mr. Scott,

766
00:33:43,260 --> 00:33:45,620
没有引擎动力 我们就会迎面撞进
without engine power, we are going to fly head-first into 

767
00:33:45,620 --> 00:33:47,160
一片巨大的伽玛射线暴
a massive gamma-ray burst,

768
00:33:47,160 --> 00:33:48,927
这样我们无法幸免
and we are not going to survive it.

769
00:33:58,304 --> 00:33:59,540
斯科特先生 我需要解决方法
Mr. Scott, I need a solution.

770
00:33:59,540 --> 00:34:01,460
呃 我可以手动
Uh... I can manually

771
00:34:01,460 --> 00:34:03,920
一点一点地把能量转给你
reroute power to you in small increments.

772
00:34:03,920 --> 00:34:05,500
这应该有点用
That should give you something.

773
00:34:05,500 --> 00:34:07,080
快 现在就做
Do it. Do it now.

774
00:34:07,080 --> 00:34:09,200
你大概有30秒的时间加速
You've got roughly 30 seconds of acceleration.

775
00:34:09,200 --> 00:34:10,740
你能做到吗
Can you make that work?

776
00:34:10,740 --> 00:34:12,280
我可以一试
I do like a good challenge.

777
00:34:32,600 --> 00:34:33,460
我们躲过了
We're through.

778
00:34:36,120 --> 00:34:37,560
希望不要再来一次爆发了
Let's hope there isn't another one.

779
00:34:39,760 --> 00:34:42,748
斯科特先生 我想跟努尼恩·辛格上尉谈谈
Mr. Scott, I'd like to talk to Lieutenant Noonien-Singh.

780
00:34:44,316 --> 00:34:47,085
呃 我看看能否接通她
Uh, let me see if I can get her.

781
00:34:49,520 --> 00:34:53,125
我们继续假设一下
Let's say I figured out a way to contact La'An.

782
00:34:53,125 --> 00:34:55,140
我找到联络拉安的办法了
Hypothetically.

783
00:34:55,620 --> 00:34:57,400
那你就是我的假设的英雄了
Then you'd be my hypothetical hero.

784
00:34:57,400 --> 00:34:58,830
我觉得你不能用老方法联系她
I think you can't get through in a conventional way

785
00:34:58,830 --> 00:35:01,000
因为人工智能屏蔽了所有
because the AI is blocking out all comms

786
00:35:01,000 --> 00:35:02,240
模拟程序以外的通讯
that don't come from the simulation.

787
00:35:02,240 --> 00:35:05,880
它拒绝让她跟任何不是程序内的人说话
It's refusing to let her talk to anyone who's not part of the program.

788
00:35:05,880 --> 00:35:06,620
它居然在进化
It's-it's... it's evolving.

789
00:35:06,620 --> 00:35:09,475
所以你需要让它相信 你也是全息投影
So you need to convince it you're a hologram, too.

790
00:35:15,040 --> 00:35:17,640
太空管辖权的书
I wrote the book

791
00:35:17,640 --> 00:35:20,080
可是我编的
on space jurisdiction,

792
00:35:20,080 --> 00:35:22,321
而我最出名的可就是
and I am known...

793
00:35:23,523 --> 00:35:26,592
语言措辞
...for my... diction.

794
00:35:26,592 --> 00:35:27,959
好了
Now...

795
00:35:27,959 --> 00:35:32,764
给我联系 艾戈尼亚人
get me... the Agonyans.

796
00:35:34,740 --> 00:35:36,320
艾戈尼亚人?
The Agonyans?

797
00:35:36,320 --> 00:35:38,540
-哦 停 -什么
- Oh... cut! - What?

798
00:35:38,540 --> 00:35:39,638
继续拍 继续拍
Keep rolling. Keep rolling.

799
00:35:39,638 --> 00:35:40,639
-好的 -是不是有点过头了
- Okay. - Was that too much? I-I...

800
00:35:40,772 --> 00:35:42,107
我觉得挺好的
I thought it was great.

801
00:35:42,107 --> 00:35:43,242
-我明白你的意思 -好的 好的
- I completely felt it. - Okay, okay, okay, okay.

802
00:35:43,242 --> 00:35:44,620
好的 在片场安静点
Okay. Quiet on the set.

803
00:35:44,620 --> 00:35:46,380
安静点
Quiet on the set.

804
00:35:46,380 --> 00:35:47,613
又有什么问题
What's the problem now?

805
00:35:47,613 --> 00:35:50,360
哦 我该怎么说呢
Oh, where do I even start? Uh,

806
00:35:50,360 --> 00:35:53,620
要不你试试着像真正的人类一样说台词
maybe you could try delivering the line like an actual 

807
00:35:53,620 --> 00:35:54,980
 哪怕就一次
human being for once?

808
00:35:54,980 --> 00:35:55,987
哦
Oh.

809
00:35:55,987 --> 00:35:58,480
好吧 要是你写的台词
Well, maybe if you wrote a line...

810
00:35:58,480 --> 00:36:01,560
值得我演个正常人 我倒乐意试试
...worth delivering, I could try to.

811
00:36:01,560 --> 00:36:03,220
这一幕到底讲的是什么
What is this scene even about?

812
00:36:03,220 --> 00:36:04,640
不是关于资本主义的吗
I thought it was about capitalism.

813
00:36:04,640 --> 00:36:06,020
这我真没想到
Big surprise.

814
00:36:06,020 --> 00:36:07,860
你没有理解剧本
You didn't understand the script.

815
00:36:07,860 --> 00:36:09,060
这都第几次了
Again.

816
00:36:09,060 --> 00:36:11,460
这里没有哪怕半个人理解我的远大图景吗
Does no one here care about my vision?

817
00:36:11,460 --> 00:36:12,304
呃 先生
Uh, sir?

818
00:36:12,304 --> 00:36:13,900
干什么
What?!

819
00:36:13,900 --> 00:36:16,107
有你的电话 呃
There's a call. Um...

820
00:36:20,260 --> 00:36:21,580
你这电话不太碰巧
Not a good time.

821
00:36:23,449 --> 00:36:25,651
什么 我
What? I...

822
00:36:27,819 --> 00:36:30,055
你不能这样 我
You can't do that. I-I...

823
00:36:30,055 --> 00:36:32,358
我成就了这部剧 你不
I am the show. You c--

824
00:36:32,979 --> 00:36:34,380
我
I...

825
00:36:34,380 --> 00:36:36,762
你会后悔的
You'll regret this.

826
00:36:41,267 --> 00:36:43,068
拉安 拉安
La'An? La'An?

827
00:36:44,800 --> 00:36:46,940
拉安 我不知道你能不能看见我
La'An, I don't know if you'll see this,

828
00:36:46,940 --> 00:36:48,774
但这是我唯一跟你联系的机会了
but it was my only chance of getting a message to you.

829
00:36:48,774 --> 00:36:50,840
全息甲板把全舰其他区域的算力
The holodeck is pulling all computer

830
00:36:50,840 --> 00:36:52,940
都快吸干了
processing power from the rest of the ship.

831
00:36:52,940 --> 00:36:55,200
我们阻止它的唯一方式就是终止程序
The only way to stop it is to end the program, 

832
00:36:55,200 --> 00:36:57,516
也就是说你得解开这个谜题
which means you have to solve the mystery.

833
00:36:58,980 --> 00:37:01,440
等等 如果我们用掉了
Wait. If we're pulling all processing power,

834
00:37:01,440 --> 00:37:04,280
包括护盾 导航和维生系统的所有算力
that includes shields, navigation, life support.

835
00:37:04,280 --> 00:37:06,720
他们会死的 我们都会死
They could die. We could all die.

836
00:37:06,720 --> 00:37:07,840
你说得很准确
An accurate assessment.

837
00:37:07,840 --> 00:37:09,328
我说得很
An accurate asse...

838
00:37:10,320 --> 00:37:11,800
你怎么能一点都不关心
How are you not more concerned?

839
00:37:11,800 --> 00:37:13,500
这关乎我们的朋友 我们的命
These are our friends, our lives.

840
00:37:13,500 --> 00:37:14,900
你要求我保持客观冷静
You asked me to remain detached.

841
00:37:14,900 --> 00:37:16,760
我只是按你的要求行事
I am merely doing as you requested.

842
00:37:16,760 --> 00:37:18,560
我们现在知道贝洛斯确实非常在乎
We now know that Bellows did indeed care very much

843
00:37:18,560 --> 00:37:19,738
剧集被砍的事
about the cancellation.

844
00:37:19,738 --> 00:37:22,660
对 这给了他动机 并且他有机会动手
Yep. That gives him motive, and he had an opportunity.

845
00:37:22,660 --> 00:37:25,560
但他没理由杀伍兹或者卢皮诺
But he had no reason to kill Woods or Lupino.

846
00:37:25,560 --> 00:37:26,460
她可没砍这部剧 
She didn't cancel the show.

847
00:37:26,460 --> 00:37:28,280
她愿意付出一切来拯救它
 She would have done anything to save it.

848
00:37:28,620 --> 00:37:30,280
确实如此
That's true.

849
00:37:30,280 --> 00:37:33,140
甚至开除我也在所不惜
Including firing me.

850
00:37:33,140 --> 00:37:36,580
真奇怪 如此鼎鼎大名的侦探
You know, for such a smart detective,

851
00:37:36,580 --> 00:37:38,500
也能犯这种蠢
you're awfully stupid.

852
00:37:38,500 --> 00:37:41,200
他们没有取消这部剧
They weren't canceling us.

853
00:37:41,200 --> 00:37:42,780
他们只是把我换掉了
They were replacing me.

854
00:37:43,245 --> 00:37:44,580
这可是我自己的剧啊
On my own show.

855
00:37:44,580 --> 00:37:47,540
或许我们应该坐下 冷静地谈谈
Perhaps we should sit down and calmly discuss this.

856
00:37:47,540 --> 00:37:51,280
我很冷静 我来这就为了要回我的工作
I came here calm. I came here to ask for my job back.

857
00:37:51,280 --> 00:37:54,760
你知道这有多羞辱人吗
Do you have any idea how humiliating that is?

858
00:37:55,560 --> 00:37:57,200
然后他拒绝了你 于是你就
And when he said no, that's when you--

859
00:37:57,200 --> 00:37:58,820
我谁都没杀啊
I didn't kill anybody!

860
00:37:58,820 --> 00:38:00,960
那就把枪放下
Then put the gun down.

861
00:38:01,760 --> 00:38:04,440
你真的会伤到人
You could actually hurt someone in here.

862
00:38:04,440 --> 00:38:05,920
这不再是个游戏了
Th-This isn't a game anymore.

863
00:38:05,920 --> 00:38:07,486
这从来不是个游戏
This was never a game.

864
00:38:09,700 --> 00:38:11,040
这是我的事业
This is my career.

865
00:38:11,780 --> 00:38:13,600
我才不要放下枪
And I'm not putting the gun down

866
00:38:13,600 --> 00:38:15,361
因为我不是杀人凶手
because I'm not the killer.

867
00:38:16,662 --> 00:38:18,964
但这里总有一个人是
But someone else here is.

868
00:38:20,080 --> 00:38:20,900
我吗
Me?

869
00:38:21,480 --> 00:38:23,640
我是被请来这查案的
I was brought here to solve this case.

870
00:38:23,640 --> 00:38:24,520
我知道
I know.

871
00:38:24,940 --> 00:38:28,420
艾米莉亚·穆恩 伟大的侦探
Amelia Moon, the great detective.

872
00:38:28,420 --> 00:38:32,120
她到哪儿 死亡就会跟到哪
Death just seems to follow her wherever she goes.

873
00:38:32,120 --> 00:38:33,420
不 这太离谱了 我
No, this is crazy. I--

874
00:38:33,420 --> 00:38:37,860
还有你这个穿着奇装异服的古怪朋友
And your strange friend in his odd clothes,

875
00:38:37,860 --> 00:38:39,740
看起来完全没有七情六欲
so devoid of emotion.

876
00:38:39,740 --> 00:38:41,987
总是在观察
Always watching,

877
00:38:43,080 --> 00:38:44,720
学习
studying.

878
00:38:44,720 --> 00:38:46,800
嘿 等等
Hey, wait a minute.

879
00:38:46,800 --> 00:38:49,027
你是电视台派来的吗
Did the network send you?

880
00:38:49,027 --> 00:38:50,629
你就是替代我的人吗
Are you my replacement?

881
00:38:53,365 --> 00:38:54,860
不 你这个蠢货
No! You idiot!

882
00:38:54,860 --> 00:38:56,368
他只是来帮我的
He was just here to help me!

883
00:38:56,368 --> 00:38:57,636
我不是 我没有
I-I didn't. I didn't.

884
00:38:59,300 --> 00:39:01,100
史波克 史波克
Spock? Spock?

885
00:39:02,320 --> 00:39:03,520
我没事
I'm okay.

886
00:39:03,520 --> 00:39:05,176
谢天谢地
Oh, thank God.

887
00:39:25,180 --> 00:39:26,598
怎么了
What is it?

888
00:39:31,460 --> 00:39:32,871
是你
It's you.

889
00:39:34,080 --> 00:39:36,180
你就是凶手
You're the killer.

890
00:39:36,180 --> 00:39:37,580
你去假装诊断系统的时候
You poisoned Lupino's cup

891
00:39:37,580 --> 00:39:40,900
在卢皮诺的杯子里下了毒
when you were "running diagnostics."

892
00:39:40,900 --> 00:39:44,640
你弄坏了吊灯 然后救了我
You sabotaged the chandelier, then saved me from it.

893
00:39:44,640 --> 00:39:47,000
然后
And then...

894
00:39:47,000 --> 00:39:48,600
你杀了伍兹
you killed Woods.

895
00:39:48,600 --> 00:39:51,760
很新颖的理论 但我没有动机
A novel theory, but I have no motive.

896
00:39:51,760 --> 00:39:54,240
我只是你的同事 协助你侦查案件
I am simply your colleague, assisting you with a case.

897
00:39:54,240 --> 00:39:55,760
你甚至不是这个故事的一部分
You're not even a part of this story.

898
00:39:55,760 --> 00:39:57,295
是我带你来这儿的
I brought you here.

899
00:40:03,160 --> 00:40:05,437
是你利用了我 你才能出现
Because you made me bring you here.

900
00:40:06,200 --> 00:40:07,960
你不是我的同事
You're not my colleague.

901
00:40:07,960 --> 00:40:10,080
你是个全息投影
You're a hologram.

902
00:40:10,080 --> 00:40:13,500
自我进入全息甲板的那一刻你就在这了
You have been since the moment I walked into the holodeck.

903
00:40:13,500 --> 00:40:16,540
我让计算机为我量身定制一个谜题
I asked the computer for a mystery made for me,

904
00:40:16,540 --> 00:40:19,220
然后你就是谜题 因为
and it gave me you, because, well,

905
00:40:19,220 --> 00:40:22,488
电脑看到了我之前和真的史波克在一起 并且
it watched me earlier with the real Spock, and...

906
00:40:25,140 --> 00:40:27,364
它知道我从不怀疑他
...it knew I'd never suspect him.

907
00:40:32,480 --> 00:40:34,980
非常精彩 拉安·努尼恩·辛格上尉
Bravo, Lieutenant La'An Noonien-Singh.

908
00:40:34,980 --> 00:40:36,800
你解决了这个谜题
You have solved the mystery.

909
00:40:42,580 --> 00:40:43,715
计算机
Computer...

910
00:40:46,000 --> 00:40:46,800
结束程序吧
...end program?

911
00:40:55,840 --> 00:40:58,500
尽管全息甲板技术确实有潜力 
While holodeck technology certainly holds promise, 

912
00:40:58,500 --> 00:41:00,580
但是风险实在是多于它的优点
the risks outweigh the potential benefits.

913
00:41:01,520 --> 00:41:05,060
我们不推荐把该装置安装在现役星舰上
We do not recommend the device be installed on active ships... 

914
00:41:05,060 --> 00:41:06,520
 目前如此
at this time.

915
00:41:06,520 --> 00:41:07,885
我们干脆建议把它用箱子锁起来
How about we recommend that it be locked

916
00:41:07,885 --> 00:41:09,420
埋进暗无天日的地里吧
in a box deep underground somewhere?

917
00:41:09,420 --> 00:41:12,337
呃 如果我可以小小的补充一下
Well, if I could just make one wee, tiny addendum.

918
00:41:12,337 --> 00:41:14,460
它只是需要一个独立的服务器机房
It-it just needs a dedicated server room

919
00:41:14,460 --> 00:41:15,941
然后供能也得是独立的
and power source that--

920
00:41:16,700 --> 00:41:19,720
记在报告里吧 不过只作为脚注
Include it in the report, but as a footnote.

921
00:41:19,720 --> 00:41:21,547
用小字体
In small print.

922
00:41:23,240 --> 00:41:24,220
中尉
Lieutenant?

923
00:41:25,180 --> 00:41:27,340
你知道在船上我们有多少船员吗
Do you know how many crew we have on board?

924
00:41:27,340 --> 00:41:28,587
呃
Uh...

925
00:41:28,587 --> 00:41:29,820
203个人
203.

926
00:41:30,580 --> 00:41:34,760
具体的讲 有整整203名星际舰队最优秀的现役军官
Specifically, 203 of the finest Starfleet has to offer.

927
00:41:34,760 --> 00:41:36,680
当你需要帮助的时候
There is never any reason

928
00:41:36,680 --> 00:41:38,660
永远没有必要独自去抗担子
to do something alone when you need help.

929
00:41:38,660 --> 00:41:40,231
是啊 但如果有呢
Yeah, but what if there is?

930
00:41:42,480 --> 00:41:44,860
在驭星者号遇上戈恩人的前一周
About a week before my last ship ran into the Gorn,

931
00:41:44,860 --> 00:41:46,972
我当时正在建传感器阵列
I was building a sensor array.

932
00:41:47,500 --> 00:41:48,780
我好像发现了一些异常
I thought I saw some anomalies,

933
00:41:48,780 --> 00:41:50,780
但是没有时间去调查它
but I didn't have time to finish it.

934
00:41:50,780 --> 00:41:53,980
我的指挥官说她会去看看 但她没有 然后我们就
My CO said she would, but she didn't, and then we...

935
00:41:57,640 --> 00:42:01,052
驭星者号的事情不是你的错
What happened on the Stardiver wasn't your fault.

936
00:42:02,300 --> 00:42:04,440
我们的工作很艰难
What we do here is hard,

937
00:42:04,440 --> 00:42:06,260
而且时常会发生不幸
and sometimes bad things happen.

938
00:42:07,540 --> 00:42:09,709
但船员们是一个团体
But this crew is a team.

939
00:42:10,520 --> 00:42:13,020
知道何时向别人寻求帮助不是什么弱点
Knowing when to ask for help isn't a weakness.

940
00:42:13,020 --> 00:42:14,566
而是一种力量
It's a strength.

941
00:42:14,566 --> 00:42:16,940
也是舰长和我非常重视的品德
One the captain and I value very highly.

942
00:42:32,617 --> 00:42:34,820
感谢你愿意来完成我们之前的课程
Thank you for agreeing to finish our lesson from earlier.

943
00:42:34,820 --> 00:42:35,640
不用谢
Of course.

944
00:42:38,560 --> 00:42:40,662
计算机 播放歌单 史波克二十一号
Computer, begin playlist: Spock 21.

945
00:42:42,040 --> 00:42:44,000
所以 我想你对全息甲板的谜题测试
So I take it the holodeck mystery test was not

946
00:42:44,000 --> 00:42:45,043
不是很满意
to your satisfaction.

947
00:42:48,080 --> 00:42:52,160
我想要的是单人向的解密
Well, I requested a solo mystery,

948
00:42:52,160 --> 00:42:55,400
但是全息甲板让我误以为我需要一个搭档
yet the holodeck led me to believe I needed a partner.

949
00:42:55,400 --> 00:42:56,808
我找了你
You.

950
00:43:04,860 --> 00:43:06,362
它误解了你的要求吗
It misunderstood your prompt?

951
00:43:07,620 --> 00:43:10,055
这个嘛 我想它理解的非常到位
That, I think it understood perfectly.

952
00:43:11,860 --> 00:43:13,260
我只是没有想到
I just didn't take into account

953
00:43:13,260 --> 00:43:15,300
全息甲板比我想的更了解我
that the holodeck knew me better than I realized.

954
00:43:16,420 --> 00:43:19,300
它给了我一个我从未设想到的嫌疑人
It gave me a suspect I never anticipated.

955
00:43:20,420 --> 00:43:21,920
十分有趣的技术
Interesting technology.

956
00:43:26,071 --> 00:43:28,206
你是怎么破除它的诱导的
How did you deduce this twist?

957
00:43:28,206 --> 00:43:29,741
我一开始真被骗到了
I didn't at first.

958
00:43:29,741 --> 00:43:31,777
完全跟着错误的线索链调查
I was looking for clues in all the wrong places.

959
00:43:33,100 --> 00:43:35,180
但我现在理解了它到底出的是什么题
But now I understand the puzzle it built for me.

960
00:43:41,040 --> 00:43:42,453
愿闻其详
And what was that?

961
00:43:42,453 --> 00:43:44,455
它用全息投影复刻了一个你
It created a holographic version of you

962
00:43:44,455 --> 00:43:46,992
头脑清晰 有逻辑
that was clear-headed, logical.

963
00:43:49,780 --> 00:43:50,696
冷漠
Cold.

964
00:44:02,360 --> 00:44:04,495
这么形容我很正确
Words that have been used to describe me.

965
00:44:05,605 --> 00:44:07,540
但我
But I...

966
00:44:07,540 --> 00:44:09,480
我了解你
I know you.

967
00:44:11,500 --> 00:44:13,840
我知道你跳舞时手臂抱着我的感觉
I know the feel of your arms when we dance.

968
00:44:13,840 --> 00:44:17,720
我知道我们注视彼此的眼神里有什么
I... know the way we look into each other's eyes.

969
00:44:17,720 --> 00:44:19,120
他看我的样子和你不同
He didn't look at me like that.

970
00:44:20,680 --> 00:44:22,961
也许我之前误判了什么
Or perhaps I've misread the situation.

971
00:44:29,920 --> 00:44:31,440
之前跳舞那次
Earlier today...

972
00:44:32,800 --> 00:44:35,373
我想知道是不是我想太多了
I wondered if it was I who had misunderstood.

973
00:44:35,373 --> 00:44:39,778
因为有那么一瞬间 我以为你想
Because for a moment, I thought that you wanted...

974
00:44:40,712 --> 00:44:44,282
那 你也想吗
And... did you also want?

975
00:45:00,993 --> 00:45:03,701
我们要吃掉人类凉皮
We will eat the human food-pies!

976
00:45:03,701 --> 00:45:06,240
是凉皮 还是粮堆来着
Is it... is it pies, or piles?

977
00:45:06,240 --> 00:45:07,420
是堆
It's piles.

978
00:45:07,920 --> 00:45:08,880
皮吗
Pies?

979
00:45:08,880 --> 00:45:10,308
向左
Left.

980
00:45:10,308 --> 00:45:13,040
回来 向右 向右
And back. Right, right, right.

981
00:45:13,040 --> 00:45:14,220
往右啊
And right!

982
00:45:16,780 --> 00:45:17,849
这个怎么样
How's this?

983
00:45:18,320 --> 00:45:19,480
这样呢
How about this?

984
00:45:20,920 --> 00:45:22,099
天杀的
Goddamn it!

985
00:45:22,099 --> 00:45:22,921
小心衣服
Costumes!

986
00:45:22,921 --> 00:45:24,890
各位 这是星云吗
You guys, is it "nebula"?

987
00:45:24,890 --> 00:45:25,760
哇哦
Whoa!

988
00:45:29,000 --> 00:45:30,560
那我们需要帮助
Then we'll need a leg up.

989
00:45:30,979 --> 00:45:32,540
-这是我的台词 -我以为这是我的台词
- That's my line! - I thought I had the leg bit.

990
00:45:32,540 --> 00:45:33,899
-台词 -什么 为什么你要讲这句
- Line? - What? Why would you have the leg bit?

991
00:45:34,032 --> 00:45:36,001
我不知道 我以为我有这句台词
I-I don't know. I thought I had the leg bit.

992
00:45:36,101 --> 00:45:37,735
这很明显是我的台词 是舰长的台词
Well, it's clearly my line! It's a captain's line.

993
00:45:37,869 --> 00:45:39,437
为什么她有这句台词
Why would she have the leg bit?

994
00:45:39,604 --> 00:45:40,738
这是我的台词
It's my line.

995
00:45:41,760 --> 00:45:42,969
是啊 我们正在等信号
Yeah. We're waiting on sound.

996
00:45:42,969 --> 00:45:45,171
红色皮革 黄色皮革
Red leather, yellow leather.

997
00:45:48,880 --> 00:45:49,939
嘿
Hey.

998
00:45:51,939 --> 00:45:53,451
我收不到她的信号了
I've lost her.

999
00:45:54,300 --> 00:45:56,154
我收不到了
I've lost her!

1000
00:45:57,500 --> 00:45:59,260
我收不到了
I've lost her!

1001
00:46:02,593 --> 00:46:06,380
老天啊 我只是想跨过这个椅子
Jesus Christ. I was trying to get my leg over.

1002
00:46:06,380 --> 00:46:08,266
这个椅子 就不能
Can... this chair...

1003
00:46:09,299 --> 00:46:11,602
有人能修下这个椅子吗 求求了
Can someone fix the chair? Please?

1004
00:46:12,280 --> 00:46:14,105
我不能坐这玩意
I'm... I w... I can't work like...

1005
00:46:14,105 --> 00:46:15,040
开门
Open the door.

1006
00:46:21,279 --> 00:46:22,547
救命 救命
Help. Help!

1007
00:46:23,520 --> 00:46:24,460
好了 我扶住你了
Yeah, I got you.

